\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-\uc2 Thai c.bank\uc2  says has acted to curb baht volatility\b0\par\par\uc2 263 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Oktober 2022\par 08:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Recasts, adds detail)\par \par \uc2 BANGKOK, Oct 1 (Reuters) - \uc2 Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to reduce \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Saturday, as the Thai baht \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hovered at 16-year lows against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The baht has fallen 11.7% against the dollar this year, which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said had been driven by dollar strength.\par \par \uc2 However, the weighted baht index against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been stable, while the country's external position and banking system remained strong, Deputy Bank of Thailand Governor \uc2 Mathee Supapongse\uc2  told reporters.\par \par \uc2 "We've entered the market sometimes to slow down volatility (in the baht)," he said, adding the \uc2 BOT\uc2  had no target for baht levels.\par \par \uc2 A fall in \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's international reserves was not because of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but rather asset valuations, he said.\par \par \uc2 Despite wide Thai-U.S. rate differentials, Thailand has attracted capital inflows, Mathee said.\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors have bought 150 billion baht ($3.97 billion) of Thai shares so far this year but sold 33 billion baht of bonds.\par \par \uc2 Governor \uc2 Sethaput Suthiwartnarueput\uc2  said gradual and measured policy tightening was suitable to support Thailand's still slow economic recovery, but he was ready to adjust if needed.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the \uc2 BOT\uc2  raised its key interest rate by a quarter point to 1.00% to tame 14-year high inflation. ($1 = 37.77 baht) (Reporting by Kitiphong Thaichareon and Satawasin Staporncharnchai; Editing by Kim Coghill Writing by Orathai Sriring Editing by Kim Coghill) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-10-1T07:49:08.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221001eia100a6p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
