\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-\uc2 Thai  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  to relax  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  rules further to curb baht rise\b0\par\par\uc2 422 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2021\par 13:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Eased \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rules for non-resident firms\par \par \uc2 * Baht has gained nearly 11% since last April\par \par \uc2 * New virus curbs could contribute to baht strength (Recasts with briefing, adds analyst's comment)\par \par \uc2 By Orathai Sriring\par \par \uc2 BANGKOK, Jan 5 (Reuters) - \uc2 Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday it plans to further relax rules on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  after easing regulations for non-resident firms, facilitating outflows of funds to contain the strong baht amid a fresh wave of coronavirus infections.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Thailand (BOT) \uc2 will review and gradually announce changes to regulations, including for property purchases overseas, director Pawinee Jitmongkolsa-mer said.\par \par \uc2 "We want to see more Thai investment abroad," she told a briefing.\par \par \uc2 The BOT has eased rules steadily to curb the baht, which has gained nearly 11% versus the dollar since April, last announcing a series of measures in November.\par \par \uc2 Earlier on Tuesday, the BOT said it had allowed non-resident companies greater flexibility to conduct baht transactions with domestic financial institutions under the non-resident qualified company scheme.\par \par \uc2 Participating non-financial firms which trade and directly invest in Thailand are allowed to manage \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks related to the baht without having to provide proof of underlying for each transaction, the BOT said in a statement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bot.or.th/Thai/PressandSpeeches/Press/News2564/n0164e.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.bot.or.th/Thai/PressandSpeeches/Press/News2564/n0164e.pdf}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 They can also manage baht liquidity without being subject to the end-of-day outstanding limit of 200 million baht ($6.68 million) imposed on non-resident baht accounts, it said.\par \par \uc2 "The measures are aimed at maintaining baht stability in the longer term," senior BOT director Chayawadee Chai-Anant said, adding that the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's had been largely driven by external factors.\par \par \uc2 Kobsidthi Silpachai, head of capital markets research at \uc2 Kasikornbank\uc2 , said new coronavirus outbreak restrictions would also hurt domestic demand and imports, adding further support for the current account surplus and the baht's strength.\par \par \uc2 He predicted the baht would appreciate to 29.00-29.25 per dollar at year-end from about 29.94 on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The BOT has repeatedly expressed concerns about the baht's gains and said would consider measures to tackle it. But analysts say market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be difficult as \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now on a \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  watch list of countries suspected of taking measures to weaken their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 29.95 baht) (Reporting by Orathai Sriring and Satawasin Staporncharnchai Editing by Martin Petty and Catherine Evans) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-1-5T13:07:19.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020210105eh1500qe1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
