\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Thai baht at 7-year high as dollar slides, c. bank seen holding back\b0\par\par\uc2 695 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 2020\par 09:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 Indonesia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  holds interest rate steady\par     * Singapore dollar climbs to a more than two-year high \par     * Thai baht hits its strongest level since late May 2013 \par \par     By Shriya Ramakrishnan\par     Dec 17 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gained ground on\par Thursday with the Thai baht surging to a seven-year peak as\par investors bet that a rebuke from Washington on Thailand's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  practices may prompt the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  not to suppress\par an appreciation in baht.\par     Regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strengthened as progress towards a U.S.\par stimulus package pushed the dollar to 2-1/2-year lows against\par major rivals. The Malaysian ringgit, Singapore dollar\par  and Indian rupee added between 0.2% and 0.4%.\par     The baht strengthened 0.4% and breached the \par psychological 30 per dollar mark that Thai exporters had urged\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to preserve last week to keep them competitive.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had then \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to slow the volatility\par in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \par     In a long-overdue report, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  added India,\par Thailand and Taiwan to a watch list of countries it suspects may\par be deliberately devaluing their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against the dollar.\par     Thailand said its addition to the list would have no big\par impact, while Taiwan said its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policies were aimed at\par stability and that it hopes to cut its trade surplus with the\par United States to address U.S. concerns.\par     Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have gained strongly against a globally\par weaker dollar since May as signs of an economic rebound in the\par region, low valuations and high yields in some markets drew a\par flood of foreign capital. \par     "In the near-term the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might refrain from\par heavily supporting the baht due to the report," said Poon\par Panichpibool, a market strategist at Krung Thai Bank.\par     "By letting the baht dip below the 30 per dollar level\par today, it is a signal that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will let it move\par more freely in line with its Asian peers."\par     The Indonesian rupiah, which backs one of Asia's most\par popular bond markets for foreign investors, held steady at\par 14,085 per dollar as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  kept its key interest rate\par unchanged at a record low of 3.75%, after five rounds of cuts\par this year.\par     Yields on the Indonesian government's ten-year bonds\par  were down 8.9 basis points after the announcement,\par while stocks in Jakarta dipped 0.2%.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also left its benchmark interest\par rate at a record low of 2%. The peso was up marginally. \par     In equity markets, Singapore shares shed 0.4%, after\par data showed the city-state's non-oil domestic exports\par unexpectedly fell 4.9% in November from a year earlier.\par \par     \par     HIGHLIGHTS:\par     ** Thailand's 10-year government bond yields are down 4\par basis points at 1.24%\par     ** Top losers on the Jakarta stock index include\par Indo-Rama Synthetics Tbk PT down 7% at 2790 rupiah;\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Multifiling Mitra Indonesia Tbk PT\f28 \uc2 \f2  down 6.88% at 745\par rupiah\par     ** Top losers on FTSE \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bursa Malaysia\f28 \uc2 \f2  Kl Index\par include \f28 \uc2 \f2 Genting Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2  down 2.07% at 4.74 ringgit; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Public\par Bank Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2  down 1.83% at 4.42 ringgit; \f28 \uc2 \f2 CIMB Group\par Holdings Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2  down 1.78% at 21.48 ringgit\par     \par   Asia stock indexes and                                  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at   0759 GMT                           \par  COUNTRY   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RIC        \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     INDEX  STOCK  STOCKS\par                       DAILY  YTD %               S   YTD %\par                           %                  DAILY  \par                                                  %  \par  Japan                +0.29  +5.26            0.18   13.32\par  China     <CNY=CFXS  -0.02  +6.58            1.13   11.63\par            >                                        \par  India                +0.19  -2.80            0.40   12.90\par  Indonesi             +0.04  -1.46           -0.24   -3.11\par  a                                                  \par  Malaysia             +0.42  +1.41           -0.51    5.29\par  Philippi             +0.05  +5.42           -0.02   -6.62\par  nes                                                \par  S.Korea   <KRW=KFTC  +0.06  +5.77           -0.05   26.06\par            >                                      