\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-\uc2 Thai c.bank\uc2  sees no 'material impact' from inclusion on US watch list\b0\par\par\uc2 320 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 2020\par 05:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds detail, finance minister's comment, baht movement)\par \par \uc2 BANGKOK, Dec 17 (Reuters) - \uc2 Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday it did not see a big impact on foreign trade and investment by being put on a U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  watch list, nor should it impede its ability to conduct macroeconomic policies to safeguard domestic stability.\par \par \uc2 The comment came after Washington put Thailand on its watch list of countries suspected of taking measures to weaken their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar\par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had conducted two-way \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  only to ride out baht volatility and had no intention to do use the exchange rate to gain an unfair trade advantage and competitiveness over trading partners, Assistant Governor \uc2 Chantavarn Sucharitakul\uc2  said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 "At this stage, the assessment is not expected to have a material impact on Thailand\u8217\'20\'19s international trade, as well as the prospect for foreign direct investment into Thailand. Similarly, such assessment does not impede the ability of the BOT to fulfill its mandate on macroeconomic policies to safeguard domestic stability," she said.\par \par \uc2 The BOT has been in close dialogue with the U.S. administration to foster an understanding of Thailand\u8217\'20\'19s macroeconomic and financial conditions, and had also reiterated its commitment to exchange rate flexibility, she said.\par \par \uc2 The baht rose 0.6% to 29.82 per U.S. dollar, breaching the psychological 30 level and at the strongest since May 2013.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister \uc2 Arkhom Termpittayapaisith\uc2  also told reporters the inclusion was "not a worry at the moment".\par \par \uc2 "It's still a monitoring list and we don't know what actions they might take. In handling the baht, it should not have any impact as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is taking care of it," he said. (Reporting by Orathai Sriring and Kitiphong Thaichareon Editing by Ed Davies) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-12-17T05:44:16.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020201217egch00izd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
