\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 The Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Thailand \highlight \highlight22\uc2 intervened \highlight\uc2  after a "too fast" rise in baht\b0\par\par\uc2 309 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 2020\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 By Kitiphong Thaichareon\par \par \uc2 BANGKOK, Nov 19 (Reuters) - \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOT) \uc2 has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in an attempt to curb the revaluation of the baht after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciated too quickly, affecting exporters, the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Sethaput Suthiwartnarueput said Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The strength of the baht, driven by news of progress in the development of a coronavirus vaccine, has exacerbated the country's fragile economic recovery, Suthiwartnarueput journalists told reporters.\par \par \uc2 Southeast Asia's second-largest economy, largely dependent on tourism and exports, contracted 6.4% in the third quarter following the fall of 12.1% in the previous quarter.\par \par \uc2 Optimism about a vaccine has raised expectations of a revival of tourism, which will boost Thailand's current account surplus and raise its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he added.\par \par \uc2 "But the reality is that we still don't know what the outcome will be. and will tourism really return?" he noted, adding that it will also depend on the availability and use of the vaccine.\par \par \uc2 "What worries us is that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has strengthened too quickly but there are no tourists yet," he explained.\par \par \uc2 The travel ban imposed in April to stop the outbreak has kept foreign tourists away. Thailand began last month to let a limited number of foreign visitors enter the country, but subject to quarantine.\par \par \uc2 The baht was trading at 30.38 per US dollar at 0606 GMT, having reached 30.13 on Monday, a peak in 10 months.\par \par \uc2 The rise in baht affected exporters, especially the smaller ones, who were already facing weak global demand, Suthiwartnarueput added. Keeping interest rates at an all-time low of 0.50% was one of the measures taken to address \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  revaluation, Suthiwartnarueput said.\par \par \uc2 (Information by Kitphong Thaichareon; written by Orathai Sriring; translation by Jorge Mart\u237\'00\'EDnez; Editing by Ed Davies)\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020201119egbj0036j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
