\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-\uc2 Thai  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to rein in  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  powered by vaccine hopes\b0\par\par\uc2 471 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 2020\par 09:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * C.bank says baht strength undermines fragile economic recovery\par \par \uc2 * Says baht rise has been too fast, hit exporters\par \par \uc2 * Bank to hold briefing on baht measures on Friday (Edits, adds investment manager quote; paragraph 9)\par \par \uc2 By Kitiphong Thaichareon\par \par \uc2 BANGKOK, Nov 19 (Reuters) - Optimism that a coronavirus vaccine will revive Thailand's devastated tourist industry has driven up the baht \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  so fast that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , its governor said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Southeast Asia's second biggest economy shrank 6.4% in the third quarter after a slump of 12.1% in the preceding quarter.\par \par \uc2 But news of promising vaccine candidates has boosted hopes for a revival in tourism to swell the current account surplus and lift the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Sethaput Suthiwartnarueput, the governor of the Bank of Thailand.\par \par \uc2 Already, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength has dealt exporters a blow, worsening Thailand's fragile recovery, he told reporters.\par \par \uc2 "But the reality is we still don't know what the result will be... and will tourism really come back?" he added, saying the outcome also hinged on vaccine availability and use.\par \par \uc2 "What we are concerned about is the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already strengthened too fast but there are no tourists yet."\par \par \uc2 The baht was trading at 30.39 per U.S. dollar by 0827 GMT, off a more than 10-month high of 30.13 on Monday.\par \par \uc2 A travel ban imposed in April to curb the outbreak has kept foreign tourists at bay. Last month, Thailand started to let a limited number of foreign visitors return, with quarantine restrictions.\par \par \uc2 "In terms of flows back in Thailand, it is still early days, but some fast money seem to be getting interested again," said Nader Naeimi, head of dynamic markets at AMP Capital, referring to hedge funds.\par \par \uc2 "It's always darkest before the dawn. It certainly felt pretty dark for Thailand only a few weeks ago."\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors have bought $1.1 billion of Thai stocks since Nov. 10 after vaccine progress was announced.\par \par \uc2 Thailand is not the only country where vaccine optimism has boosted the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Chinese state banks have also been active in yuan markets to try to rein their nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Over the past five years, \uc2 the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the baht markets when appropriate, lifting international reserves by $100 billion, the governor said.\par \par \uc2 Keeping the policy interest rate at a record low of 0.50% was one step taken to deal with the baht's strength, Sethaput said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will hold a briefing on baht measures and capital movement on Friday, he added. ($1=30.36 baht)\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Tom Westbrook in Sydney; Writing by Orathai Sriring Editing by Matthew Tostevin and Clarence Fernandez) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-11-19T09:39:48.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020201119egbj00rs1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
