\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Most Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  firm as comments on US-China spat ease worries\b0\par\par\uc2 662 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Mai 2019\par 08:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Thai baht hits a more than 2-mth high\par     * Indian rupee firms; April inflation at 6-mth high\par     * Indonesian rupiah weakens ahead of April trade data\par \par  (Updates prices, adds table)\par     By Niyati Shetty\par     May 14 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  firmed on\par Tuesday as conciliatory comments from the United States and\par China reduced investor anxiety over the escalating tariff war\par between the world's two biggest economies.\par     The Chinese yuan was largely unchanged at 6.878 a\par dollar, following a 0.9% decline on Monday.\par     Market sentiment was buoyed after U.S. President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald\par Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2  said he feels trade talks between Beijing and Washington\par are "going to be very successful", while China's top diplomat\par said the two nations have the "ability and wisdom" to reach a\par deal.\par     The comments came the day after China said it would impose\par higher tariffs on most U.S. imports on a revised $60 billion\par target list, in retaliation for the tariff hike on $200 billion\par worth of Chinese goods that went into effect from last Friday.\par \par     Investors are latching on to any twist and turn in the trade\par war negotiations, said Wei Liang Chang, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mizuho\par Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 , adding that there is less negativity in the markets now\par after the expected Chinese retaliation was announced.\par     Leading gains in the region, the Thai baht firmed\par 0.7%, hitting its strongest level in more than two months.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the best performer in the region this year,\par has had some insulation from the trade dispute due to Thailand's\par large current account surplus. \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said on Monday it has not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par in trading of the baht to gain a trade advantage with the United\par States.\par     This is positive. Chang said, as it means the authorities\par would not be restraining gains by the baht unnecessarily.\par     The Indian rupee gained 0.1% to 70.44 a dollar.    \par     Government data late on Monday showed India's retail\par inflation rate hit a six-month high in April but remained below\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's target for the ninth month.\par     The Philippine peso and the Singapore dollar\par firmed against the greenback, and the South Korean won\par  was little changed. \par     \par     RUPIAH's PRE-DATA STUMBLE\par     Indonesia's rupiah weakened as much as 0.3% to 14,450\par per dollar ahead of April trade figures on Wednesday and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank\par Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2 's interest rate decision on Thursday. \par     The country is expected to record its first trade deficit in\par three months in April, according to a Reuters poll, with exports\par and imports predicted to continue their plunge.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is expected to keep the benchmark rate at\par 6% as Sino-U.S. trade tensions have put pressure on the rupiah.\par \par     \par     \par  Change on the day at 0609 GMT                    \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                Latest bid  Previous day  Pct Move\