\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Most Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  firm as comments on US-China spat ease worries\b0\par\par\uc2 489 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Mai 2019\par 07:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Thai baht hits a more than 2-mth high\par \par \uc2 * Indian rupee firms; April inflation at 6-mth high\par \par \uc2 * Indonesian rupiah weakens ahead of April trade data (Adds text)\par \par \uc2 By Niyati Shetty\par \par \uc2 May 14 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed on Tuesday as conciliatory comments from the United States and China reduced investor anxiety over the escalating tariff war between the world's two biggest economies.\par \par \uc2 The Chinese yuan steadied 0.1% to 6.873 a dollar, following a 0.9% decline on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Market sentiment was buoyed after U.S. President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said he feels trade talks between Beijing and Washington are "going to be very successful", while China's top diplomat said the two nations have the "ability and wisdom" to reach a deal.\par \par \uc2 The comments came the day after China said it would impose higher tariffs on most U.S. imports on a revised $60 billion target list, in retaliation for the tariff hike on $200 billion worth of Chinese goods that went into effect from last Friday.\par \par \uc2 Investors are latching on to any twist and turn in the trade war negotiations, said Wei Liang Chang, \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Mizuho Bank\uc2 , adding that there is less negativity in the markets now after the expected Chinese retaliation was announced.\par \par \uc2 Leading gains in the region, the Thai baht firmed as much as 0.5% to 31.46 per dollar, hitting its strongest level in more than two months.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the best performer in the region this year, has had some insulation from the trade dispute due to Thailand's large current account surplus.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday it has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trading of the baht to gain a trade advantage with the United States.\par \par \uc2 This is positive. Chang said, as it means the authorities would not be restraining gains by the baht unnecessarily.\par \par \uc2 The Indian rupee gained 0.2% to 70.4 a dollar.\par \par \uc2 Government data late on Monday showed India's retail inflation rate hit a six-month high in April but remained below the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target for the ninth month.\par \par \uc2 The Philippine peso and the Singapore dollar firmed against the greenback, and the South Korean won was marginally stronger.\par \par \uc2 RUPIAH's PRE-DATA STUMBLE\par \par \uc2 Indonesia's rupiah weakened as much as 0.3% to 14,450 per dollar ahead of April trade figures on Wednesday and \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2 's interest rate decision on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The country is expected to record its first trade deficit in three months in April, according to a Reuters poll, with exports and imports predicted to continue their plunge.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to keep the benchmark rate at 6% as Sino-U.S. trade tensions have put pressure on the rupiah.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Niyati Shetty in Bengaluru; Editing by Richard Borsuk) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2019-5-14T06:54:20.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020190514ef5e00rmh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
