\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-\uc2 Thai c.bank\uc2  says has not manipulated  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  for trade advantage\b0\par\par\uc2 286 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Mai 2019\par 09:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, trade data and baht)               \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK, May 13 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the trading of the baht to gain a trade advantage with the United States,  an assistant governor said on Monday, amid speculation that Washington may soon add the country to a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  watch list.               \par \par \uc2 "Thailand has some trade surplus with the United States, so it could be on the watch list," Chantavarn Sucharitakul said in a text message to reporters.               \par \par \uc2 But, "\b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  has always communicated that it has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for an advantage in trade with the United States," she said, adding that it was open for further discussions.               \par \par \uc2 Her comments come after a report that an expanded \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  watch list expected this month could include Russia, Thailand, Indonesia, Vietnam, Ireland or Malaysia, all of which have large trade surpluses with the United States.               \par \par \uc2 Thai authorities have said in the past they will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to "smooth out" any excessive moves in the baht. Exports are a key driver of Southeast Asia's second-largest economy.               \par \par \uc2 The United States had a goods trade deficit of $4.3 billion with Thailand in January-March this year, after a deficit of $19.3 billion in the whole of 2018, according to \uc2 U.S. Census Bureau\uc2 .               \par \par \uc2 In the first quarter of 2019, the United States was Thailand's biggest export market, accounting for 14.2 percent of Thai shipments, Thai customs data showed.               \par \par \uc2 The baht has appreciated by 2.8 percent against the greenback so far this year, making it the best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia.               \par \par \uc2 Released: 2019-5-13T08:32:42.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020190513ef5d00zkm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
