\par\par \b \uc2 Thai c.bank\uc2  says it has  \highlight22\uc2 intervened \highlight\uc2  to slow baht strengthening\b0\par\par\uc2 183 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Dezember 2017\par 06:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK, Dec 12 (Reuters) - \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday it has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year to slow the baht's strengthening to soften impact on businesses.\par \par \uc2 "Many external factors this year have strengthened the baht too quickly" \uc2 the Bank of Thailand\uc2  said in a statement, adding that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was "not in line with economic fundamentals of the country."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not give details of how and when it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "\uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in to ensure that the baht does not appreciate too quickly to soften impact on businesses," the statement said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expects pressure on the baht to ease due to a lower current account surplus and increasing public and private investments as the economy recovers, the statement said.\par \par \uc2 It also said the baht appreciation will not impact export growth but business profits will be affected.\par \par \uc2 In 2017, the baht has strengthened nearly 10 percent against the dollar. (Reporting by Kitiphong Thaichareon; Writing by Chayut Setboonsarng; Editing by Richard Borsuk) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-12-12T06:06:41.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020171212edcc008hm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
