\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Thais to be allowed to invest more abroad as  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  rules eased\b0\par\par\uc2 359 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 2017\par 11:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, quotes)\par \par \uc2 By Orathai Sriring and Kitiphong Thaichareon\par \par \uc2 BANGKOK, June 5 (Reuters) - \uc2 Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday it would relax \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rules, including taking steps to allow more Thais to invest in securities abroad, in a move that analysts said could help contain an uncomfortably strong baht \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will allow investors with assets of at least 50 million baht ($1.47 million) to directly invest in securities abroad of up to $1 million per year, effective by the end of 2017, it said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Commercial banks will also be allowed to lend baht to non-residents for investment in Thailand and the Greater Mekong sub-region, effective this month, it said.\par \par \uc2 "The moves are aimed at enhancing ease of doing business and will not affect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's responsibility to maintain financial stability," Bank of Thailand Veerathai Santiprabhob told a news conference.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said the measures would help counter some of the baht's strength, and help exports needed to generate faster economic growth.\par \par \uc2 The baht, however, hit a near 23-month high of 33.94 per dollar after the measures were announced, as investors had been expecting stronger steps.\par \par \uc2 The baht has appreciated by more than 5 percent against the dollar this year, making it the best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Southeast Asia.\par \par \uc2 "Despite the baht's strength, it's still moving in line with regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and with economic fundamentals. Its volatility remains low - in mid range of the region. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is monitoring it closely," assistant governor Vachira Arromdee said reporters.\par \par \uc2 Though interest rates are at a record low of 1.5 percent, Thailand is running a hefty current account surplus and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves have risen by $12 billion this year to stand at $184 billion.\par \par \uc2 A $29 billion balance on \uc2 the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s forward book, however, hints at heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to keep the baht from appreciating even further. ($1 = 34.00 baht) (Editing by Simon Cameron-Moore) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-6-5T10:39:18.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020170605ed6500el4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
