\par\par \b \uc2 *Bank of Thailand Keeps Benchmark Rate Unchanged At 1.5%\b0\par\par\uc2 420 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 November 2016\par 08:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 9 Nov 2016 02:17 ET *Bank of Thailand: Despite Greater Downside Risk, Thai Economy Still Expanding at Same Rate as Previously Assessed\par \par \uc2 9 Nov 2016 02:17 ET *Bank of Thailand: Tourism, Private Consumption Expected to Slow Down Temporarily\par \par \uc2 9 Nov 2016 02:18 ET *Bank of Thailand: Effect of Stronger Baht on Trade, Economic Recovery Still of Concern\par \par \uc2 9 Nov 2016 02:18 ET *Bank of Thailand: Will Preserve Policy Space to Deal with Future Uncertainties\par \par \uc2 9 Nov 2016 02:18 ET *Bank of Thailand: Focus Remained on Economic Conditions at Latest Policy Meeting\par \par \uc2 9 Nov 2016 02:19 ET *Bank of Thailand: Monetary Policy Committee Looks at Uncertainties from U.S. Election Results\par \par \uc2 9 Nov 2016 02:19 ET *Bank of Thailand: Too Soon to Assess Impact of U.S. Presidential Election Result\par \par \uc2 9 Nov 2016 02:20 ET *Bank of Thailand: New U.S. Policies Related to Global Trade Need to Be Monitored After Election\par \par \uc2 9 Nov 2016 02:22 ET *Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 : No Comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 9 Nov 2016 02:29 ET  \uc2 Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Leaves Policy Rate Unchanged\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Nopparat Chaichalearmmongkol \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BANGKOK--\f28 \uc2 \f2 Thailand's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  left interest rates unchanged Wednesday despite concerns over a slowdown in economic activity as the country mourns the death of King Bhumibol Adulyadej.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2 's monetary policy committee voted unanimously to leave the one-day repurchase rate untouched at 1.5% for the 12th consecutive meeting.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The bank's decision was in line with the views of 16 economists polled by The Wall Street Journal. Most analysts played down the recent lull in activity as a short-term phenomenon that won't affect an underlying recovery in the economy, especially in exports and imports.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Following the death of the monarch on Oct. 13, the junta-installed government requested the country suspend all festive activities for one month and declared a one-year mourning period.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The bank has taken a cautious stance on policy, arguing that rates are already sufficiently supportive of the economy. The BOT is also seen wanting to maintain policy ammunition should the global economy weaken or if \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  decisions elsewhere, including a possible rate increase in the U.S., affect the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  or capital flows.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Thai \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last cut rates in April 2015.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Nopparat Chaichalearmmongkol at nopparat.chaichalearmmongkol@wsj.com.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 November 09, 2016 02:29 ET (07:29 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020161109ecb9000yv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
