\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Baht hits 13-month high vs dollar, buoyed by inflows\b0\par\par\uc2 611 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 2016\par 09:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Baht hits highest level since July 2015\par     * Won supported by dollar-selling by local exporters\par     * Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  steady to firmer ahead of Yellen's speech\par \par  (Updates prices, adds text)\par     SINGAPORE, Aug 26 (Reuters) - The Thai baht touched a\par 13-month high on Friday, supported by recent inflows into local\par bonds and equities, while the South Korean won edged higher on\par dollar-selling by local exporters.\par     Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were generally steady to firmer against the\par dollar ahead of U.S. Federal Reserve Chair \f28 \uc2 \f2 Janet Yellen\f28 \uc2 \f2 's\par speech, which could provide hints on when the Fed will raise\par interest rates.\par     Yellen's speech at the Fed's annual conference in Jackson\par Hole, Wyoming is due at 1400 GMT. \par     "Given prevailing market scepticism, any reference to\par phrases like 'the next meeting' being 'live' would undoubtedly\par precipitate a U.S. dollar surge," Emmanuel Ng, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 OCBC Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 , said in a note.     \par     The Fed has kept interest rates on hold after raising them\par last December, its first hike in nearly a decade, and\par uncertainty remains on  whether it will increase rates this\par year.\par     According to \f28 \uc2 \f2 CME Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 's FedWatch tool, U.S. interest rate\par futures are now implying a 21 percent chance of the Fed raising\par interest rates in September, and about a 52 percent chance of a\par hike by December.\par     \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par     The rupiah edged higher on Friday, but was down 0.6\par percent for the week, a decline that analysts say may have been\par exacerbated by dollar-buying by overseas bond investors hedging\par their exposure to the Indonesian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .    \par     \par     THAI BAHT\par     The baht touched a peak of around 34.50 versus the\par dollar at one point, its highest level since July 2015.\par     Market participants said the baht was supported by fund\par inflows into Thai equity and bond markets.\par     There was some wariness among dealers, however, about the\par risk of Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb gains in the baht.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor said on Tuesday that a\par rapid rise in the baht was not good for the country's economic\par recovery although it was not causing exports to decline.\par  \par     \par     SOUTH KOREAN WON\par     The won advanced on local exporters' demand, although its\par gains were capped ahead of Yellen's speech in Jackson Hole.\par     The won edged up 0.2 percent in onshore trade. \par  \par        \par   Change on the day at   0727 GMT                        \par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                Latest bid   Previous   Pct Move\par                                            day  \par   Japan yen                  100.44     100.52      +0.08\par   Sing dlr                   1.3518     1.3533      +0.11\par   Taiwan dlr                 31.660     31.670      +0.03\par   Korean won                1112.90    1115.90      +0.27\par   Baht                        34.53      34.57      +0.10\par   Peso                       46.335     46.350      +0.03\par   Rupiah                    