\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Rises on Hawkish Fed Speak-- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,800 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juli 2015\par 02:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.2076-6.2102    6.2043-6.2355 \par USD/TWD   31.240-31.330    31.150-31.500 \par USD/KRW    1,140-1,150      1,135-1,160 \par USD/SGD   1.3600-1.3692    1.3561-1.3750 \par USD/MYR   3.8040-3.8300    3.8000-3.8500 \par USD/THB    34.01-34.20      33.86-34.42 \par USD/PHP    45.18-45.25      45.05-45.36 \par USD/IDR         -                - \par USD/INR    63.45-63.57      63.34-63.87 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--consolidation. USD/CNY is still stuck in a narrow range of 6.2051-6.2102; technical momentum is lacking unless this range breaks and the pair enters the Bollinger downtrend or uptrend channels. Overnight U.S. dollar index strength - due to hawkish overtones from \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  chief \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  in her testimony on monetary policy - could lead to a higher daily USD/CNY benchmark rate set by the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2 , which typically acts as a beacon for spot USD/CNY. The yuan has been steady of late, likely due to authorities keeping volatility in check, amidst wild fluctuations in the stock market. The benchmark Shanghai Composite Index may slide back down after Wednesday's lower closing affirmed the daily Bollinger downtrend channel - a bearish technical signal. Stocks fell even though China's second-quarter GDP data beat expectations, rising 7.0% versus forecasts for a rise of 6.8%. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/CNY is at 6.2076 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 6.2051 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 6.2043 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is at 6.2102 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 6.2127 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 6.2355 (weekly Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--uptrend. USD/TWD is likely to keep rising now that the Bollinger uptrend channel has been activated. The uptrend channel supports the dollar at 31.240 and could lead toward the weekly Bollinger uptrend channel at 31.420 in the days ahead. The U.S. dollar rose overnight on comments from U.S. Federal Reserve chief that an interest rate increase this year might be appropriate if the economy performs according to the Fed's expectations. Bullishness for the greenback was affirmed in the offshore market Wednesday, where the price of the benchmark 1-month USD/TWD nondeliverable forward contract rose to 0.010 above the spot contract price, versus Tuesday's discount of 0.020. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 31.240 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 31.150 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 31.080 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 31.330 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 31.420 (weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), before 31.500 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--uptrend. USD/KRW opens higher Thursday, marking a new two-year high, as the greenback rallies broadly on a hawkish stance in U.S. Federal Reserve chief \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2 's testimony on monetary policy Wednesday. USD/KRW is fast approaching the 1,150 round-figure trading barrier which if breached might trigger a short-covering spike higher. The street is now bracing for a U.S. interest rate rise in September - which would have the effect of boosting the U.S. dollar due to covering of carry-trade positions - after Ms. Yellen said a rate increase this year would be appropriate if the economy continues to perform as the Fed expects. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,140 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 1,135 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1,130 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is at 1,150 (round-figure trading barrier), before 1,160 (round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--uptrend. USD/SGD touched a three-month high overnight on hawkish comments from the U.S. Federal Reserve, and is likely to keep climbing toward the round-figure trading barrier of 1.3700. The daily USD/SGD has been bullish since three sessions ago, and the weekly chart could soon turn bullish as well if the pair closes Friday above 1.3696 and thus in the weekly Bollinger uptrend channel. The greenback is broadly higher after a hawkish stance was projected in U.S. Federal Reserve chief \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2 's testimony on monetary policy Wednesday. The growing likelihood of a September U.S. rate increase is spooking U.S. dollar shorts - who are borrowing cheaply in U.S. dollars to sell it for higher-yielding assets in emerging markets. Data released Thursday showed Singapore's non-oil domestic exports rose 4.7% on-year, versus a median forecast of 2.0%, but had little impact on USD/SGD due to the overarching theme of a stronger U.S. dollar ahead. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.3600 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 1.3561 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1.3500 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is at 1.3692 (weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.3700 (round-figure trading barrier), before 1.3750 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--uptrend. USD/MYR is likely to keep rising - if the \uc2 Malaysia \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stops \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market to limit ringgit weakness - as the greenback rallies across the board. Hawkish comments from U.S. Federal Reserve chief \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  in her testimony on monetary policy Wednesday has sent the U.S. dollar significantly higher. Bullish technical cues also suggest USD/MYR will keep climbing; the pair is inside the daily Bollinger uptrend channel which now supports at 3.8040. Additional pressure on the ringgit may come from the recent drop in crude oil prices - partly due to the Iran nuclear sanctions deal - which threatens Malaysia's oil export revenues. This could have a negative impact on Malaysia's economy and its trade balance in the medium to long term. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.8040 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.8000 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 3.7800 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 3.8300 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.8500 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--uptrend. USD/THB is on its way up again, as the greenback receives a fresh boost from indications by the U.S. Federal Reserve chief that a rate increase this year is on the cards. The dollar hit a new six-year high versus the Thai baht overnight, but could struggle to climb much higher during the Asian trading session on speculation that \uc2 the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  has recently been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market to slow the baht's decline. On Wednesday, U.S. Federal Reserve chief \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  raised expectations for a September interest rate increase in her testimony on monetary policy. She said that a rate increase would be appropriate if the economy continues to perform as expected. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 34.01 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 34.00 (round-figure trading barrier), before 33.86 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is at 34.20 (psychological resistance), before 34.42 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--uptrend. USD/PHP is likely targeting a near-term top of 45.36 - the ceiling of the weekly Bollinger uptrend channel. The daily Bollinger uptrend channel supports USD/PHP at 45.18; as long as this technical floor holds, the pair appears likely to keep rising in the near term. The greenback is generally stronger as markets reacted to the U.S. Federal Reserve's hint of a U.S. interest rate increase this year. Fed chief \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  in her testimony on monetary policy Wednesday said that a rate increase may be appropriate if the economy continues to perform as forecast. Riskier emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are especially vulnerable to a U.S. rate increase because a rise in USD-funding costs might spur capitulation of the short-USD carry trade. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is 45.18 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 45.13 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 45.05 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 45.25 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 45.36 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), before 45.50 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--closed.\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--consolidation, possible uptrend. USD/INR is slated to open higher on the back of broad U.S. dollar strength triggered by hawkish comments from U.S. Federal Reserve chief \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  in her testimony on monetary policy Wednesday. USD/INR could turn mildly bullish if it ends Thursday above 63.57 and thus inside the Bollinger uptrend channel. A clean break of the 63.87 ceiling of the Ichimoku Cloud consolidation zone is needed to chart a more bullish outlook for USD/INR. The overnight drop in crude oil prices could however thwart a USD/INR rally. Cheaper oil in the medium to long term is expected with the Iran nuclear sanctions deal, which is beneficial for India's current account deficit and thereby the rupee. India's rupee has in the past suffered due to investor concern over its large current account deficit - mainly due to expensive energy imports. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 63.45 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 63.34 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 63.22 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 63.57 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 63.69 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 63.87 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 15 Jul 2015 20:56 ET  USD/Asia Rises on Hawkish Fed Speak-- Asia Daily -2-\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 . The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 July 15, 2015 20:56 ET (00:56 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150716eb7g0000t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
