\par\par \b \uc2 Thai Exporters Seek Relief From Strong Baht\b0\par\par\uc2 By Warangkana Chomchuen and Nopparat Chaichalearmmongkol \par \uc2 661 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Februar 2015\par 14:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK--Thailand's main business group urged the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to tamp down the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying its strength is hurting exports as they struggle to bounce back from two years of negative growth.\par \par \uc2 The Thai baht has been relatively resilient over the past 13 months despite weak domestic growth and a political crisis that led to a military coup d'\u233\'00\'E9tat in May.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has strengthened 0.83% against the U.S. dollar since the start of this year, trading at 32.64 baht to the dollar Wednesday. \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of other Southeast Asian nations, including Singapore, Indonesia and Malaysia, have weakened as much as 3% against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2015.\par \par \uc2 This has put Thai exporters at a disadvantage as a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  makes the country's goods more expensive for buyers, Isara Vongkusolkit, chairman of the Thai Chamber of Commerce, said after meeting with officials from the \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We have to lower our prices to be competitive with neighboring countries who export similar products," Mr. Isara said. Such a move cuts into businesses' profits.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  has likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at times to keep the baht stronger to try to avert capital outflows amid concerns about an expected U.S. Federal Reserve rate increase, said Charl Kengchon, managing director at Kasikorn Research. Such a move by the Fed could spark fund outflows from emerging markets such as Thailand,where bondholdings by overseas investors total as much as 600 billion baht ($18.38 billion), added Mr. Charl.\par \par \uc2 The country's current-account surplus and large holdings of U.S. dollars have contributed to the baht's relative strength in the region.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to $155.4 billion by the end of January compared with $166.8 billion in January of last year, according to the \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The baht's strength has added yet another challenge to the recovery of Thai exports. Overseas shipments, which account for about two-thirds of the country's gross domestic product, contracted 0.41% last year, compared with a 0.32% decline in 2013, the Commerce Ministry reported.\par \par \uc2 Falling agricultural prices, lower shipments of oil and declining global demand have already weighed on the outlook for exports this year amid the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation experienced by Thailand's major trade partners, including the \uc2 European Union\uc2  and Japan.\par \par \uc2 The strong baht "is certainly not a crisis right now, but it's something that we encourage the \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  to look into because the impact is likely going to be long-term," said Vichai Assarasakorn, vice chairman of the Thai Chamber of Commerce, which didn't specify what it considered to be an appropriate exchange rate. The group also urged the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the use of local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in border trades instead of a reliance solely on the U.S. dollar, Mr. Vichai said.\par \par \uc2 Pongpen Ruengvirayudh, deputy governor of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said at a news conference after the meeting that the bank would do its best to address the concerns about the strong baht, but ruled out issuing new \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures.\par \par \uc2 "We will do everything with our available monetary tools to ensure that the baht isn't posing a big obstacle for exporters," she said.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Pongpen cautioned, however, that monetary policy has limitations, and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  is only one of the challenges to the country's exports. The global economic slowdown and weakening demand have already put pressure on Southeast Asian exporters, she said.\par \par \uc2 So far, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't noticed any sign of speculative baht trading, she said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  has estimated exports would grow 1% this year.\par \par \uc2 Write to Warangkana Chomchuen at warangkana.chomchuen@wsj.com and Nopparat Chaichalearmmongkol at nopparat.chaichalearmmongkol@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 February 11, 2015 08:18 ET (13:18 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150211eb2b00387\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
