\par\par \b \uc2 Thailand  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  to Assure Baht Stability -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 147 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 2014\par 13:08\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 1108 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  vows to maintain the stability of the Thai baht following calls from the military government to rein in the value of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "So far, the baht movement has not caused any problem to Thailand's trade or investment," says Prasarn Trairatvorakul, governor of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "The BOT will stand ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the value of the baht weakens or strengthens too much and too fast in order to prevent any impact on local economy." Since the beginning of 2014, the baht has strengthened nearly 2% against the dollar, according to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (nopparat.chaichalearmmongkol@dowjones.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 July 15, 2014 07:08 ET (11:08 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140715ea7f001c4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
