\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Thailand Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Denies Pressure for Baht  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,473 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juli 2014\par 12:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1047 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Thailand's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  denies it is facing pressure from the military government to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market to boost the economy, which is expected to grow 1.5% in 2014. "Right now, I can confirm that no one [from the junta] has asked us to do anything with the baht," says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  Gov. Prasarn Trairatvorakul, referring to news reports that the junta wants the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stabilize at 32 to a dollar, which is considered competitive. The baht has strengthened 1.1% since the May 22 coup to 32.22 per dollar on Wednesday. (nopparat.chaichalearmmongkol@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 1033 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--Inflationary pressures are absent in the Czech economy, with the June year-on-year consumer price index stagnating at zero after a 0.4% rise in May. "I see the only positive in the June inflation figure and that it wasn't negative," says Raiffeisenbank analyst Vaclav France. Looking forward there could be some increase of inflation in July but mostly thanks to the low year-ago base, Mr. France says. "The June inflation data increases the likelihood of the (\uc2 Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) delaying the exit from its weak-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime until the end of next year," he says. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said it is resolved to maintain the EUR/CZK at levels above 27.00 at least through April 2015. EUR/CZK is trading at 27.45 at midday, up from 27.43 late Tuesday. (leos.rousek@wsj.com, @LeoRousek)\par \par \uc2 1021 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Economists, investors and Indian citizens are likely hoping that the country's new government can make major steps toward upgrading India's crumbling infrastructure. But Rajiv Lall, executive chairman of the infrastructure-finance firm IDFC, says tomorrow's budget announcement, the Narendra Modi government's first, can be good for infrastructure even if it doesn't contain loads of new state spending on big projects. Lall said that the important first step the government could take to help the sector is to make it easier to get financing. That requires, among other things, recapitalizing the giant state-owned banks, which have been in a poor state largely due to earlier infrastructure-related loans that have turned toxic amid India's economic slowdown. "Existing balance-sheet issues need to be sorted out first before corporate India will return to health," Lall said. (raymond.zhong@wsj.com, \uc2 Twitter\uc2 : @zhonggg)\par \par \uc2 1018 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--The strength of the New Zealand dollar has surprised \uc2 Barclays\uc2 , as the U.K. clearer had looked for the $0.88 area to cap the Kiwi's current advance. However, the bullish breakout seen Tuesday has turned the bank neutral. A daily close Wednesday above $0.88 will flip its view to bullish, targeting the 1982 post-float high of $0.8845, with $0.90 as a longer-term target. Now trading at $0.8805. (gary.stride@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1011 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Germany's auction of two-year debt, known as Schatz, Wednesday delivered some eye-catching numbers, following the trend set by the nation's football team in Brazil last night! Firstly, the 0.01% average yield represented the lowest two-year German borrowing cost since an auction in January 2013, when it was also 0.01%. Secondly, the average and minimum accepted prices matched, hence the auction didn't have a "tail", which is a sign of strong demand. Thirdly, the bid-to-cover ratio of 2.5, is the second highest year-to-date at a two-year German auction. (emese.bartha@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1007 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Stocks of Indonesian palm oil companies listed overseas and domestically look to gain once election fever subsides and a new government gets down to business, says Alvin Tai, Malaysia based analyst with RHB Research Institute Bhd. The Indonesia exchange was closed during election day, but stocks of Singapore-listed Indonesia firms gave an indirect read on the vote. According to early and unofficial counts, Joko Widodo was leading by a narrow margin. \uc2 Bumitama Agri Ltd\uc2 . (P8Z.SG), \uc2 Golden Agri-Resources Ltd\uc2 . (EH.SG) and \uc2 Indofood Agri Resources Ltd\uc2 . (5JS.SG) opened higher on the FTSE Straits Times Index earlier in the day. \uc2 Bumitama Agri\uc2  finished the day 0.4% higher at S$1.265 a piece, while the remaining two ended flat at S$0.555 and S$0.975 respectively. "Regardless of who wins the elections, for the plantation sector it is positive as the new government will have to start implementing its biodiesel program, which had slowed due to elections," says Tai. (venkat.pr@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0946 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--\uc2 Commerzbank\uc2 's London technical team held a bearish view on the Swedish krona even before the Riksbank surprised with a 50 bps rate cut last week. That event helped their view along, and recent price action suggests krona weakness will now extend throughout the rest of 2014. For USD/SEK there may be some consolidation around 6.86-6.87, but any dips to 6.80-6.77 are seen as a buy to target 7.00. USD/SEK now at 6.82. (gary.stride@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0945 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--A long sterling position remains a high-conviction trade in the market, but one major risk here is extended positioning, notes \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2 . Using its own \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  positioning analysis, GBP longs are now running at +43 on a scale of +50 to -50 and are by far the largest single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exposure within G10. EUR positioning, however, has only just moved into negative territory with a score of -16, so the bank says running short EUR/GBP positions looks a safer bet for those with a positive sterling conviction. EUR/GBP is now at 0.7956. (gary.stride@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0937 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--Builders in Bahrain have scaled back construction of office buildings, but oversupply in the local office market remains high and rents are depressed, consultancy Knight Frank says in a note. There are signs that office rents have "found a floor," but prime rents are still around 40% below their 2008 peak, Knight Frank says. Development activity is expected to remain depressed in the next 12 months and vacancy rates are elevated. Newer buildings in prime locations are nevertheless doing fairly well, but old buildings that are laid out inefficiently are set to do poorly, Knight Frank says. (asa.fitch@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0936 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--\uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  expects Hungary's headline price index to remained -0.1% on the year in June. "Price dynamics should remain very similar to what we saw in May, with inflation kept negative by a deep decline in food prices, substantial cuts in utility prices, and generally stable core inflation," it adds. Hungary's headline inflation index is set to remain close to zero or marginally negative until end-3Q, especially as the next, small cut in utility prices, mandated by the government, comes in September, Goldman adds. After that, inflation will start to increase owing to utility price cuts of a year earlier "dropping out" from the index, Goldman notes. Forecasts Hungary's inflation will accelerate to 1.3% by end-2014 and reach the country's 3.0% inflation target by mid-2015. June's CPI reading is due at 0700 Friday. (margit.feher@wsj.com @margitfeher)\par \par \uc2 0934 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--\uc2 Danske Bank\uc2  recommends investors to invest in Ireland's EUR500 million auction of its 3.40% March 2024 bond Thursday, the only Irish bond auction in 3Q. Danske's chief analyst Jens Peter Sorensen and senior analyst Anders Moller Lumholtz expect \uc2 Fitch Ratings\uc2  to upgrade Ireland on Aug. 15 on the back of stronger growth, better budget figures and tentative signs of improvement in the banking sector. And after \uc2 Moody's\uc2  upgrade of Ireland into investment grade, they would expect a second single-A rating over time to drive further performance of Irish bonds, as this would mean Irish bonds benefit from index inclusion and a broader investor base. (emese.bartha@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0932 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The USD/PHP hits a fresh eight-month low late Wednesday, reflecting the dollar's broad weakness against other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and steady fund inflows to the local market. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pair is at 43.315 after settling late Tuesday at 43.405. A local bank trader says the market awaits Federal Reserve minutes for trading cues. Volume is light. Traders expect the USD/PHP to move between 43.20 and 43.60 in the near term. (cris.larano@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 July 09, 2014 06:47 ET (10:47 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140709ea79001cm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
