\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -U.S. data, weak yuan drag Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 ; baht steady on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 785 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Mai 2014\par 07:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Thai c.bank spotted limiting baht's losses -traders\par     * Philippine peso falls as maturing NDFs boost dollar demand\par     * Singapore dlr up on exporters, 55-day moving avg support\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, May 28 (Reuters) - The Philippine peso led losses\par among emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Wednesday, pressured by\par upbeat U.S. economic data and a weaker Chinese yuan, while the\par Thai baht recovered most of its initial losses - with \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spotted.\par     The peso hit a near three-week low, tracking its\par weakness in the non-deliverable forwards (NDF) market\par .\par     Indonesia's rupiah fell on importers' dollar demand\par for month-end payments.\par     Spot Chinese yuan flirted with fresh 18-month lows against\par the dollar as investors focused on negative news from the\par property sector as further evidence of a slowdown in the\par economy. \par     The dollar held steady around an eight-week high\par against a basket of six major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after data showing U.S.\par durable goods sales unexpectedly rose in April and consumer\par confidence perked up in May. \par     Still, analysts said the data has not prompted the U.S.\par Federal Reserve to consider an early interest rate hike yet, so\par emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may not weaken further.\par     "On a one-month time horizon, I would buy Asia. The recent\par sell-off has created good entry points for long (positions),"\par said Sean Yokota, head of Asia strategy at Scandinavian bank SEB\par in Singapore.\par     "We have some profit-taking into the month-end after good\par performance in INR and CNY," Yokota said, referring to the\par Indian rupee and the yuan.\par     Last week, the rupee hit an 11-month high on hopes the\par recent landslide election victory of the Bharatiya Janata Party\par would bring in a government willing to undertake substantial\par economic reform.\par     Emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have benefited extensively from\par monetary easing by major central banks as investors sought out\par higher returns from EM assets.\par  \par      PHILIPPINE PESO\par     The peso fell as much as 0.4 percent to 43.965 per dollar,\par its weakest since May 8 when \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  raised the\par Philippines' rating to two notches above investment grade.\par  \par     Dollar demand linked to maturing NDFs put pressure on the\par peso, traders said.\par     "It is better to be long (dollar) on dips close to 43.85,"\par said a senior Philippine bank trader in Manila, adding the\par peso's slides accelerated after it weakened past 43.83, its low\par on May 21.\par         \par     BAHT\par     The baht eased 0.1 percent to 32.67 per dollar, its weakest\par since Feb. 19, tracking weakness in other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The Thai \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , however, recovered all of the losses as\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was spotted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  around the low to curb\par the falls, traders said.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's imports in April dropped 14.54 percent from a\par year earlier, indicating reduced dollar demand from local\par importers. \par     Factory output fell for a 13th straight month in April, and \par  even though the slide was less than expected it underscored the\par extent of economic damage from the prolonged political unrest.\par  \par     \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par     The Singapore dollar gained on month-end demand\par from domestic companies such as exporters.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also has a chart support at 1.2565, a 55-day\par moving average. It has been closing the daily session firmer\par than average since March 25.\par     Still, some hedge funds sold the Singapore dollar and a\par weaker yuan limited its gains.\par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0440 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       101.93         101.98       +0.05\par   Sing dlr        1.2553         1.2565       +0.10\par   Taiwan dlr      30.111         30.171       +0.20\par   Korean won     1022.30        1023.20       +0.09\par   Baht             32.65          32.63       -0.06\par   Peso             43.94          43.78       -0.36\par   Rupiah        11605.00       11575.00       -0.26\par   Rupee            59.14          59.04       -0.17\par   Ringgit         3.2195         3.2170       -0.08\par   Yuan            6.2586         6.2486       -0.16\par  \par   Change so far in 2014\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       101.93         105.28       +3.28\par   Sing dlr        1.2553         1.2632       +0.63\par   Taiwan dlr      30.111         29.950       -0.53\par   Korean won     1022.30        1055.40       +3.24\par   Baht             32.65          32.86       +0.64\par   Peso             43.94          44.40       +1.04\par   Rupiah        11605.00       12160.00       +4.78\par   Rupee            59.14          61.80       +4.50\par   Ringgit         3.2195         3.2755       +1.74\par   Yuan            6.2586         6.0539       -3.27\par  \par  (Additional reporting by Satawasin Staporncharnchai; Editing by\par Eric Meijer)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-5-28T06:37:28.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140528ea5s0060q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
