\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Spikes as Stock Markets Slump -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,452 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Februar 2014\par 01:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY         --             -- \par USD/TWD         --             -- \par USD/KRW     1,080-1,090     1,076-1,096 \par USD/SGD    1.2740-1.2782   1.2700-1.2800 \par USD/MYR    3.3420-3.3500   3.3200-3.3620 \par USD/THB     32.80-32.98     32.62-33.13 \par USD/PHP     45.21-45.45     45.01-45.50 \par USD/IDR    12,220-12,278   12,100-12,340 \par USD/INR     62.42-63.00     62.37-63.50 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trend lines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--closed.\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--closed.\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--retreat and consolidation. USD/KRW is slightly overbought based on the U.S. unit's overextension past the upper Bollinger band (standard deviation 2) technical resistance at 1,085. The dollar may soon retreat if profit-taking of long dollar positions kicks in. Adding to mild dollar downside potential the U.S. dollar index slipped overnight owing to benchmark \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yields subsiding. Escalating risk aversion may, however, keep won strength at bay and thus support USD/KRW on dips toward the round-figure support at 1,080. Asia stocks are starting the day in the red on the heels of the large drop in U.S. equities overnight. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,080 (psychological support), then at 1,076 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1,070 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 1,090 (psychological resistance), then at 1,096 (monthly Bollinger mid resistance), before 1,100 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--supported. USD/SGD may consolidate around its current level propped up by the 20-day Bollinger midline--a technical support for the U.S. dollar. Investors' risk appetite deteriorated again overnight after a weak U.S. ISM manufacturing report that sank U.S. stocks and sent bonds higher. The rally in bonds depressed the \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  benchmark yields which may lend a slightly softer tone to the U.S. dollar preventing USD/SGD from rallying. If risk aversion continues to worsen the Singapore dollar may see more demand as investors seek stability and USD/SGD may be weighed even lower. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2740 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 1.2700 (psychological support), before 1.2698 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1.2782 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2800 (psychological resistance), before 1.2824 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--upside bias. USD/MYR is likely to head higher toward 3.3730 led by the steepening trajectory of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel--implying more weakness for the ringgit. Emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are likely to be under pressure as international risk aversion intensifies and investors turn to traditional safe-haven assets like U.S. bonds and the U.S. unit. USD/MYR is currently supported around 3.3420 by the base of the Bollinger uptrend channel and may spike higher if stop-loss orders above the 3.3500 round-figure trading barrier are triggered. Traders will however be on the lookout for possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that will deter further speculative dollar buying. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.3420 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.3200 (psychological support), before 3.3110 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is at 3.3500 (psychological resistance), then at 3.3620 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.3730 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--potential upside bias. USD/THB appears to be going nowhere on the charts for now but the stalemate may be broken if the dollar ends Tuesday above 32.98 and within the daily Bollinger uptrend channel. The political crisis in Thailand continues as the government delays releasing election results owing to obstruction of voting in several districts. If USD/THB ends the day above 32.98 dollar bulls may be convinced that more upside is coming and may add to speculative demand for the dollar. The fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has kept the baht well behaved so far--one reason why the baht has held its value against its peers as international risk aversion escalates. The \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  is believed to be capping USD/THB at 33.10-33.15 and has very large offers placed near those levels to prevent the dollar from rising against the baht. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at then at 32.80 (psychological support), then at 32.61 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 32.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 32.98 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 33.00 (psychological resistance), before 33.13 (4-year high).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--upside bias. USD/PHP is heading back up to the top of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel at 45.57 as risk aversion intensifies led by U.S. stocks sliding more than 2.0% overnight. A new 3.5-year low for the peso may be notched if USD/PHP rises past 45.45. The catalyst for the deterioration in investor sentiment was the very poor U.S. ISM manufacturing report. The international risk-off scenario developing is turning more \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders bullish on traditional safe-haven assets like the U.S. dollar and the Japanese yen. Traders are, however, wary of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Philippines \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem excessive losses for the peso. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 45.21 (monthly Ichimoku Cloud support), then at 45.01 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 45.00 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 45.45 (Monday's 3.5-year peak), then at 45.50 (psychological resistance), before 45.57 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--upside bias. USD/IDR is likely to rise higher on the bullish technical signal that emerged Monday. The daily Bollinger uptrend channel is now in effect, supporting the dollar at 12,220 and aiming it toward the intraday technical resistance at 12,340. The dollar is stronger in Asia despite \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yields dropping overnight--a classic risk-aversion setup where investors dump high-yield, emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stocks for the safety of U.S. bonds. The emerging market rout that began two weeks ago is now turning into a vicious cycle of international risk aversion that will further erode emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 12,220 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 12,200 (psychological support), before 12,100 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is at 12,278 (5-year high), then at 12,300 (psychological resistance), before 12,340 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--upside bias. USD/INR is well supported by the Ichimoku Cloud support zone--which nearly coincides with the technical support at the base of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel--and is likely to rally on the overnight rise in risk aversion. U.S. stock markets fell overnight casting a bearish tone on Asian stock markets that is also weighing on emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The dollar may find some resistance at 62.84 where the top of the uptrend channel currently caps but if dollar-buying momentum takes USD/INR past the round-figure trading barrier of 63.00 there may be a spike higher owing to stop-loss orders triggered that may augment the dollar's upward momentum. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 62.42 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 62.37 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support), before 62.00 (20-day Bollinger mid support and psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 62.84 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 63.00 (psychological resistance), before 63.50 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 February 03, 2014 19:44 ET (00:44 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140204ea240000w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
