\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Rebounds After Fed Cuts QE Again -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,339 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Januar 2014\par 01:41\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY          -               - \par USD/TWD          -               - \par USD/KRW          -               - \par USD/SGD    1.2730-1.2772   1.2700-1.2800 \par USD/MYR    3.3300-3.3470   3.3200-3.3590 \par USD/THB     32.93-33.00     32.80-33.13 \par USD/PHP     45.21-45.45     45.00-45.48 \par USD/IDR    12,070-12,220   12,000-12,278 \par USD/INR     62.44-63.00     62.37-63.50 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--closed.\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--closed.\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--closed.\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--possible upside bias. USD/SGD rose overnight as the U.S. dollar rebounded after the U.S. Federal Reserve announced a second consecutive reduction in bond buying, which brought back a tone of risk aversion in global markets. The downturn of the Turkish lira overnight, which had recovered after emergency interest rate hikes in Turkey on Tuesday, also added to jittery investor sentiment. If USD/SGD ends Thursday above 1.2772, the daily Bollinger uptrend channel could resume its bullish effect on the greenback and lead the way to 1.2823. A mitigating factor that could help the Singapore dollar hold its own is the safe haven status of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  relative to regional emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . If risk aversion escalates again, the Singapore dollar could see more demand as investors seek stability and USD/SGD could thus be weighed lower. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2730 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 1.2700 (psychological support), before 1.2684 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1.2772 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2800 (psychological resistance), before 1.2823 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--upside bias. USD/MYR is back inside the daily Bollinger uptrend channel, indicating further gains for the dollar are likely. The USD/MYR might rally toward 3.3590 where the top of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel awaits. The greenback rebounded against the emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight after the U.S. Federal Reserve again reduced its monthly bond buying program by $10 billion, sparking a bout of risk aversion in U.S. stocks. The ringgit could come under further pressure as the recent emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  selloff threatens to return after Turkey's lira experienced fresh risk aversion overnight--eroding gains made when the \uc2 Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hiked rates aggressively on Tuesday. \uc2 Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its interest rate policy unchanged on Wednesday as expected, saying that growth momentum is expected to continue in 2014. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.3300 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.3200 (psychological support), before 3.3000 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 3.3470 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.3500 (psychological resistance), before 3.3590 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--upside bias. A bullish technical signal for the USD/THB appears as the dollar edged higher due to broad risk aversion sending investors to the perceived safety of the greenback. If USD/THB ends the day above 32.93, the dollar bulls could be convinced that more upside is coming and could hence add to speculative demand for the dollar. The fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has kept the baht well-behaved so far, even as the emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  selloff brews and the political protests in Bangkok escalate ahead of the election scheduled on Feb. 2. The \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  is rumoured to be capping USD/THB at 33.10-33.15 and has very large offers placed near those levels to prevent the dollar from rising against the baht. This has been deterring speculative attacks on the baht, which has been trading in a narrow range of 32.75-33.00 for the past week. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 32.93 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 32.80 (psychological support), before 32.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 33.00 (psychological resistance), before 33.13 (4-year high).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--upside bias. USD/PHP is heading back up to the top of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel as risk aversion returns, sparked by the U.S. Federal Reserve again reducing its pace of monthly bond purchases by another $10 billion. The greenback could rise to 45.49 unless the Philippines \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  steps in to stem losses for the peso. Though the \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yields fell overnight--which typically weighs on the dollar--the U.S dollar is stronger in Asia as emerging market jitters return. The decline in the U.S. bond yields was attributed to investors' risk aversion sending them into bonds versus equities. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 45.21 (monthly Ichimoku Cloud support), then at 45.00 (psychological support), before 44.93 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 45.45 (Monday's 3.5-year peak), then at 45.48 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 45.50 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--possible upside bias. USD/IDR is likely to rally toward the entrance of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel at 12,220 following a return of emerging market jitters--triggered by another $10 billion reduction in the U.S. Federal Reserve's pace of bond buying. If USD/IDR ends Thursday above 12,220, the dollar has greater potential to rally further in the days ahead, possibly to the top of the uptrend channel at 12,360. Investors are likely also worried by the shaky recovery of the Turkish lira, which could implode again. Earlier this week, the lira triggered risk aversion in Asia as investors feared that the Indonesia rupiah could be the next target for speculative investors looking to profit from the emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rout. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 12,070 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 12,000 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 12,220 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 12,278 (5-year high), before 12,300 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--upside bias. The daily chart indicates that USD/INR has found strong support at the Ichimoku Cloud support zone and is more likely to head back up toward 63.00. The dollar may gain additional technical momentum to rally if it ends Thursday above 62.44 and thereby inside the daily Bollinger uptrend channel. The rebound of USD/INR overnight hints at strong underlying demand for the U.S. dollar. This could be due to the U.S. Federal Reserve's decision on Wednesday to again cut back on its monthly bond purchases, and also partly due to the shaky recovery of the Turkish lira--which had sparked risk aversion in Asia this week. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 62.44 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 62.37 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support), before 62.02 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is likely at 62.87 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 63.00 (psychological resistance), before 63.50 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 29, 2014 19:41 ET (00:41 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140130ea1u0006n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
