\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rupiah near 5-year low; baht caught in political fray\b0\par\par\uc2 931 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 November 2013\par 03:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Indonesian c.bank spotted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support rupiah     * Baht down on politics; \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  suspected     * Ringgit at 2-mth low on hedge funds, speculators   (Adds text, updates prices)     By Jongwoo Cheon     SINGAPORE, Nov 27 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah hit a near five-year low on Wednesday on increasing month-end dollar demand from local companies, while most emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  eased in line with a weaker yen.    Thailand's baht fell on outflow pressures due to  rising political tensions at home and weaker-than-expected exports data, while the Malaysian ringgit slid to its lowest in almost two months as hedge funds sold it.     Such declines came even as the dollar broadly fell against a basket of six major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after weaker-than-expected U.S. consumer confidence in November.      Still, the U.S. housing market provided a more encouraging reading with permits for future home construction rising to a near 5-1/2-year high.\par \par \uc2       "A strong dollar trend remains intact with underlying views of Fed tapering and a weaker yen supporting the trend," said Jeong My-young, Samsung Futures research head in Seoul.     "That continues to hurt Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . There will be more domestic issues such as Thailand's protests," Jeong added.     The Indian rupee, however, bucked regional weakness on corporate dollar inflows. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     \par     RUPIAH\par     The rupiah lost 0.7 percent to 11,835 per dollar,\par its weakest since March 2009.\par     The official Jakarta Interbank Spot Dollar Rate (JISDOR)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 , which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  introduced in May as part of a\par bid to manage exchange rate fluctuations, was fixed at 11,813\par rupiah per dollar, the weakest since JISDOR's introduction.\par     The Indonesian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell in non-deliverable forwards\par (NDFs) market on selling from offshore funds and leveraged\par accounts, traders said.\par     The rupiah's one-month NDFs also slid to\par 11,835 to the greenback, its weakest since Sept. 6, indicating\par further depreciation.\par     "At the current pace (of the rupiah's depreciation), I dare\par not say no," a Jakarta-based trader when asked if the spot\par rupiah would weaken past 12,000 per dollar this week.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was spotted providing dollar liquidity to\par support the rupiah in the local market, although traders\par preferred to sell it.\par     "The rupiah is still bearish. However, I don't want to do\par prop trading from this level, but to buy dollars from exporters\par and hold the positions," another trader in Jakarta said,\par referring to proprietary trading.\par     Due to Indonesia's current account deficit, the rupiah is\par regarded as the Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  most vulnerable to capital\par outflows once the U.S. Federal Reserve finally starts winding\par down a stimulus strategy that has fuelled dollar inflows to\par emerging markets.\par     Indonesia's president said economic growth in the fourth\par quarter was expected to be at its slowest pace in more than four\par years if the Fed starts trimming its massive bond-buying\par programme. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     \par     BAHT\par     The baht dipped on escalating political tensions and\par disappointing trade data, while its downside was limited as the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was suspected of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , traders said.\par     On Tuesday, thousands of protesters surrounded \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Interior Ministry and forced the evacuation of four others,\par intensifying their campaign to bring down the government of\par Prime Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Yingluck Shinawatra\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \par     Thai October exports slid 0.7 percent from a year earlier,\par missing market expectations of 0.7 percent growth, the\par government data showed. \par     Until the political tensions ease, "we are likely to see\par downside pressure on Thai equities, bonds and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as\par markets continue to price in a political risk premium,"\par Scotiabank said in a client note.\par     Investors were awaiting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's monetary policy\par meeting later in the day when the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  is expected\par to keep its policy rate unchanged at 2.50 percent.\par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     \par     RINGGIT\par     The ringgit fell as much as 0.3 percent to 3.2315 to the\par greenback, its weakest since Oct. 2 on selling from macro funds\par and interbank speculators.\par     Some traders covered short positions when it was weaker than\par 3.2300.\par     Still, the Malaysian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may weaken to 3.2533, the 61.8\par percent Fibonacci retracement of its appreciation between August\par and October, if it clears the 50.0 percent level at 3.2283. \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0435 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\