\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Supported Despite Dollar Index -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,753 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 November 2013\par 01:49\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.0900-6.1000   6.0802-6.1030 \par USD/TWD   29.560-29.660   29.500-29.710 \par USD/KRW    1,058-1,060     1,053-1,063 \par USD/SGD   1.2495-1.2528   1.2464-1.2568 \par USD/MYR   3.2100-3.2300   3.2000-3.2370 \par USD/THB    32.00-32.20     31.80-32.39 \par USD/PHP    43.63-43.80     43.33-43.89 \par USD/IDR   11,700-11,770   11,600-11,800 \par USD/INR    62.12-62.77     62.00-63.00 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--consolidation. The overnight slippage in the USD index could weigh the PBOC USD/CNY central parity rate slightly lower, but spot USD/CNY is likely to remain very stable. The recently less volatile spot market appears to be flatlining; the dollar has only fluctuated within a 10-pip range this week. This may deter speculative bets on the yuan and may thus keep the USD/CNY in a narrow range of 6.0900-6.0950. There are some punters who are placing bets in the NDF market for a stronger yuan benchmark exchange rate towards end-December, as the PBOC typically sets the parity rate higher for the yuan at year-end. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 6.0900 (psychological support), then at 6.0894 (entrance of Bollinger downtrend channel), before 6.0802 (record low). Immediate resistance is at 6.1000 (psychological resistance), before 6.1030 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--consolidation. The dollar needs to break above the daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone, which caps at 29.710, in order to rally. If it fails to breach this level, USD/TWD consolidation within the Cloud range of 29.500-29.710 will likely continue. A daily close within the Bollinger uptrend channel that begins at 29.660 could add to upside momentum and help steer the dollar toward the Cloud ceiling. The USD index slipped a tad overnight on poorer-than-expected U.S. consumer confidence data, though U.S. home prices rose more than expected. The NDF market is showing a tinge of bullishness for the greenback, as the benchmark 1-month NDF discount shrinks. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 29.560 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 29.500 (psychological support and base of Ichimoku Cloud), before 29.460 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 29.676 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 29.710 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--consolidation. USD/KRW is likely to bob within a band of 1,058-1,063 again as the greenback consolidates broadly. The dollar has been in this range for the past five sessions and needs to close outside of it for a stronger directional cue. If USD/KRW ends the day below 1,058, the dollar may gain downside momentum toward the psychological barrier at 1,050. On the other hand a Wednesday close above 1,063 could open the way to the Bollinger uptrend channel that begins at 1,067. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,058 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1,053 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1,060 (psychological resistance), then at 1,063 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), before 1,067 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--upside bias. The uptrend carries on for a fourth day as USD/SGD grinds higher toward the weekly Ichimoku Cloud at 1.2568. Though the USD index eased overnight on downbeat U.S. consumer confidence data, the upside bias for USD/SGD will remain as long as it stays above 1.2495, which is the base of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel. Data released Tuesday showed Singapore's October industrial production rose 8.0% on year, which was short of expectations for a rise of 9.3%. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2495 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2464 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 1.2444 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is at 1.2528 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2568 (top of weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone), before 1.2598 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--upside bias. The daily Bollinger uptrend channel is steering USD/MYR toward the top of the daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance at 3.2370, as the market appears to defy overnight dollar weakness. The uptrend channel will remain in play as long as USD/MYR closes Wednesday above 3.2100. Traders in Asia appear to be wary of a possible U.S. Federal Reserve reduction in monetary stimulus in the near future, and thus prefer to buy the dollar on dips. Overnight, the dollar softened on weaker-than-expected U.S. consumer confidence data, despite a stronger-than-forecast rise in home prices. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.2100 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.2000 (psychological barrier), before 3.1980 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud). Immediate resistance is at 3.2300 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.2370 (top of Ichimoku Cloud resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--upside bias. USD/THB is building on its rally past the psychological barrier of 32.00 and could soon surpass the Sept. 6 high of 32.48, which was a 3-year peak. Baht weakness is likely to persist even though the greenback eased overnight. The main reason for baht weakness is the month-long anti-government protest in Thailand, which has been hampering investor confidence. There are no signs that embattled Prime Minister Yingluck Shinawatra intends to give in to protestors' demands that she resign. USD/THB could next reach for the top of the weekly Bollinger uptrend channel at 32.39 --unless the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  steps in to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will announce later today its Monetary Policy decision, though this is expected to be a non-event. Thailand's trade data for October will be released at 0230 GMT. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 32.00 (psychological support), then at 31.80 (psychological support), before 31.67 (Ichimoku Cloud support zone). Immediate resistance is at 32.20 (psychological resistance), then at 32.39 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), before 32.48 (Sept. 6 high).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--retreat lower. On an intraday basis, USD/PHP could retreat toward the base of the Bollinger uptrend channel at 43.63 as upside momentum runs out. However, if the dollar ends Wednesday above this mark, the uptrend channel remains in play, which means the bullish bias for USD/PHP will resume. The turnaround in the dollar, which was triggered by a second failed attempt Monday to break above the Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone, may extend slightly further due to the overnight slippage in the USD index. Lacklustre U.S. consumer confidence data released Tuesday has been blamed for the weaker USD. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 43.63 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 43.33 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud). Immediate resistance is likely at 43.80 (psychological resistance), then at 43.89 (top of Ichimoku Cloud and top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 44.00 (psychological barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--upside bias. The rupiah may be feeling some peer pressure as regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also slip despite broad USD weakness. The rupiah could surpass the 4.5-year low of 11,790 printed Tuesday due to expectations of the U.S. Fed reducing monetary stimulus. U.S. home prices, one of the factors that the Federal Reserve considers in making a decision to reduce monetary stimulus, rose more than expected Tuesday. Ratings agency Fitch is downbeat on the Indonesian economy, lowering its growth forecast for next year's Gross Domestic Product to 5.3% from 5.5% in 2013. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 11,700 (psychological support), then at 11,600 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 11,500 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 11,770 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 11,790 (4.5-year high), before 11,800 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--consolidation. USD/INR may stabilize within a range of 62.12-62.77 after having lost its bullish bias when it fell out of the Bollinger uptrend channel. \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yields slipped and the dollar eased slightly overnight on poorer-than-expected U.S. consumer confidence data, which could keep USD/INR pinned to the lower side of the suggested trading range. The rupee has rallied this week, bucking regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , likely because of the drop in oil price which is seen as a boon to the India economy and helpful in reducing the current account deficit. But consistent demand for the U.S. dollar from onshore oil importers may keep USD/INR supported on dips. The deputy governor of the Reserve Bank of India on Monday said that a 'big chunk' of oil importers are back in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market buying dollars, as the government's scheme to allow them to buy USD directly from the RBI gets gradually removed. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 62.12 (20-day Bollinger mid support and base of Ichimoku Cloud), then at 62.00 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 62.77 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 63.00 (psychological trading barrier), before 63.42 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 26, 2013 19:49 ET (00:49 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131127e9br0003p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
