\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rupiah off lows on surprise rate hike; baht rebounds\b0\par\par\uc2 852 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juni 2013\par 03:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Indonesia c.bank hikes benchmark rate 25 bps to 6 pct     * One-month dollar/rupiah NDFs rebound     * Thai c.bank sold dlrs to support baht last week - gov   (Adds text, updates prices)     By Jongwoo Cheon     SINGAPORE, June 13 (Reuters) - The ailing Indonesian rupiah recovered some lost ground after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  surprisingly hiked the benchmark rate, while most emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  slipped on continuing worry about a possible cut in monetary stimulus.     The Thai baht, however, rebounded as the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to limit the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide last week.     The rupiah was as weak as 9,895 to the dollar until the rate hike, which strengthened it to 9,870. But in spite of the 25 basis point hike to 6.0 percent, the rupiah's spot indicated price eased 0.2 percent to 9,875 as of 0740 GMT.        \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2 's surprise hike "was a pleasantly surprise.\par \par \uc2  I think they want to send a clear message to markets that they will act on IDR weakness," said Sean Yokota, head of Asia strategy at Scandinavian bank SEB in Singapore.     "We are waiting for the Fed on next Thursday. If Bernanke remains dovish, it can reverse the IDR's depreciation trend," Yokota said.     The Federal Reserve is scheduled to open a policy meeting  June 18 and the next day Chairman \uc2 Ben Bernanke\uc2  will hold media briefing, which will take place early Thursday in Asia.     The Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's unexpected move came two days after it surprisingly hiked its overnight deposit facility rate (FASBI) by 25 basis points to 4.25 percent to try to bolster the rupiah.      The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday it was ready to ensure large supplies of dollars and to buy government bonds in the secondary market.       Still, the rupiah is unlikely to escape from a bearish mood as investors stay concerned over the Fed tapering monetary stimulus, traders and analysts said.     One-month dollar/rupiah non-deliverable forwards  rebounded after falling on the rate hike.     "The rate hike today may not be able to stem capital outflow when markets are attempting to achieve a new equilibrium in an environment of a roll back of monetary policy easing by the Fed," said Suresh Kumar Ramanathan, head of regional interest rate and \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at CIMB Investment Bank in Kuala Lumpur.     "The usual short-term reprieve - of a day or two - will allow marginal appreciation of IDR, but does not alter the view that markets have currently, that is, capital reversal to economies with stronger growth trajectory and economies with a clear signal of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation, which is the U.S. economy and the U.S. dollar," he said.     Among emerging Asian markets, Indonesia and India are the most vulnerable to capital outflows due to worries about their sizable current account deficits.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     \par     BAHT\par     The baht turned higher as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor said\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  last week sold dollars to support the Thai\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par     Governor Prasarn Trairatvorakul said he was not worried\par about recent moves in the baht and that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would\par ensure stability in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Earlier on Thursday, the baht fell on capital outflows with\par Bangkok stocks hitting a near six-month low.\par     Foreign investors sold a combined net $1.1 billion of Thai\par stocks in the month to June 12.\par         \par     RINGGIT\par     The ringgit slid on dollar demand from custodian banks amid\par weaker stocks, while domestic importers bought the greenback for\par payments.\par     Hedge funds sold the Malaysian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , traders said.\par     But investors hesitated to sell the ringgit more on caution\par over possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     On Tuesday, the ringgit hit 3.1570 per dollar, its weakest\par since July 30, 2012.\par         \par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR   \par   Change on the day at 0740 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen        94.12          95.99       +1.99\par   Sing dlr        1.2563         1.2564       +0.01\par   Taiwan dlr      29.911         30.160       +0.83\par   Korean won     1134.16        1133.60       -0.05\par   Baht             30.90          30.94       +0.13\par   Peso             43.18          43.20       +0.05\par   Rupiah         9875.00        9855.00       -0.20\par   Rupee            58.39          57.79       -1.03\par   Ringgit         3.1440         3.1315       -0.40\par   Yuan            6.1413         6.1335       -0.13\par  \par   Change so far in 2013\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen  