\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Philippine peso, baht fall on c.banks; China PMI hits Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 802 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 April 2013\par 03:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Philippine c.bank seen cutting SDA rates on Thursday\par \par \uc2  * Baht down on hedge funds selling after c.bank remarks\par \par \uc2  * Won dips as \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  suspected - traders \par \par \uc2 (Adds text, updates prices)\par \par \uc2  By Jongwoo Cheon\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, April 23 (Reuters) - The Philippine peso and the Thai baht fell on Tuesday as caution grew over \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves to stem \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation, while concerns about China's weak growth hurt emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  The peso slid on selling by offshore funds as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is widely expected to cut the rate on its short-term special deposit account (SDA) facility again on Thursday in another move to temper the peso, traders said.\par \par \uc2  "The dollar remained supported on offshore demand. Speculation of a 50 basis point (bps) or higher cut in SDA rates put pressure on the peso," said a senior Philippine bank trader in Manila.\par \par \uc2  Last month, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut by 50 basis points to 2.5 percent the rate on all its three SDA tenors.\par \par \uc2  Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinasis has lowered the SDA rate by a total of more than 150 basis points since July 2012 to encourage banks to lend more to consumers and discourage dollar flows that pushed the peso to become the second best performing emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year.\par \par \uc2  On April 18, it liberalised rules on foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions on Thursday, allowing residents to invest in property abroad and offshore funds. \par \par \uc2  The peso was not the only emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fall on caution over \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities.\par \par \uc2  The baht slid after a \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  assistant governor told Reuters on Monday that the \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  is worried about the baht's rapid rise but is unlikely to impose "draconian" measures to rein it in. \par \par \uc2  The South Korean won also eased as the authorities were suspected of selling the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to protect export competitiveness amid the yen's weakness, traders said.\par \par \uc2  A preliminary survey showing growth in China's vast factory sector dipped in April also weighed on Asian markets, suggesting the world's second-largest economy still faces formidable global headwinds in the second quarter. \par \par \uc2  BAHT\par \par \uc2  The baht slid as hedge funds reduced bullish bets on the best-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  assistant governor comments.\par \par \uc2  Paiboon Kittisrikangwan said the baht has started to move close to "a zone beyond the fundamentals" and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was ready to do something if it went "way beyond" that.\par \par \uc2  Investors grew more wary over potential \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although they have not seen it in the market yet, traders said.\par \par \uc2  "They were in the market when dollar/baht went below 28.60," said a Thai bank trader, adding the odds of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  have increased, given the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's concerns.\par \par \uc2  WON\par \par \uc2  The won eased as the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities were suspected of selling the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially when it was firmer than 1,120 per dollar, traders said.\par \par \uc2  Foreign investors continued to sell Seoul shares on worries about growth in China, which is South Korea's top export market.\par \par \uc2  They have been net sellers in the country's main exchange for am eighth consecutive session, unloading a combined net 1.2 trillion won ($1.1 billion) during the period, according to the Korea Exchange data.\par \par \uc2  Still, the won recovered some of losses on exporters' demand, traders said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par \par \uc2  Change on the day at 0740 GMT\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        98.61          99.29       +0.69\par  Sing dlr        1.2405         1.2403       -0.02\par  Taiwan dlr      29.816         29.870       +0.18\par  Korean won     1120.63        1119.00       -0.15\par  Baht             28.78          28.69       -0.33\par  Peso             41.35          41.21       -0.34\par  Rupiah         9722.00        9715.00       -0.07\par  Rupee            54.33          54.14       -0.35\par  Ringgit         3.0530         3.0490       -0.13\par  Yuan            6.1774         6.1826       +0.08\par  Change so far in 2013\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        98.61          86.79      -11.99\par  Sing dlr        1.2405         1.2219       -1.50\par  Taiwan dlr      29.816         29.136       -2.28\par  Korean won     1