\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Baht firmer, poised for best quarter in 2-1/2 years\b0\par\par\uc2 607 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2013\par 03:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Dollar/baht down more than 4 pct in Jan-March\par \par \uc2 * Baht on track for best quarter since July-Sept 2010\par \par \uc2 * S.Korean won slips as govt slashes forecast\par \par \uc2 (Adds comments, updates levels)\par \par \uc2 By Masayuki Kitano\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, March 28 (Reuters) - The Thai baht edged higher on Thursday and was on track for its best quarterly gain in 2-1/2 years as the country's upbeat economic fundamentals helped spur fund inflows into Thai equities and bonds.\par \par \uc2 Other emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mostly steady to firmer against the dollar on Thursday, although the South Korean won slipped as the country's new government sharply cut this year's growth target.\par \par \uc2 The dollar slipped about 0.2 percent to 29.25 versus the Thai baht.\par \par \uc2 With one more trading session left in the quarter, the dollar is down roughly 4.4 percent versus the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the greenback's biggest quarterly percentage decline against the baht since the July-September quarter of 2010.\par \par \uc2 Inflows into Thai equities and bonds have helped to lift the baht, which hit a 16-year high of 29.07 on March 20.\par \par \uc2 "From the yield perspective, I think risk-adjusted yields are still fairly attractive. So that should support the baht," said Andy Ji, Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist for \uc2 Commonwealth Bank of Australia\uc2  in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 When taking into account the low implied volatility of the baht, Thai bond yields hold some attraction for overseas investors, Ji said.\par \par \uc2 The macro-economic backdrop for the baht, however, seems relatively neutral at this stage, he said, adding that the baht may take a bit of a breather in the April-June quarter.\par \par \uc2 "Most of Asia is doing actually quite well so in that sense it doesn't really stand out," Ji said, adding that he expects the baht to be trading at 29.20 at the end of June.\par \par \uc2 Investors are also cautious about the potential for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem further appreciation in the baht to help exporters. On Thursday, Thailand reported that February exports fell 5.8 percent from a year earlier.\par \par \uc2 The following table shows the position of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar at 0716 GMT.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 Markets in the Philippines were closed on Thursday for a holiday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par         \par                                                        \par  Change on the day at   0716 GMT                         \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        94.18          94.45       +0.29\par  Sing dlr        1.2426         1.2429       +0.02\par  Taiwan dlr      29.894         29.941       +0.16\par  Korean won     1112.50        1111.60       -0.08\par  Baht             29.25          29.30       +0.17\par  Peso             40.80          40.80       +0.00\par  Rupiah         9712.00        9724.00       +0.12\par  Rupee            54.34          54.37       +0.05\par  Ringgit         3.0970         3.0990       +0.06\par  Yuan            6.2142         6.2140       -0.00\par                                                        \par  Change so far in                                        \par 2013                           