\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Baht retreats on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  caution; Taiwan dlr, ringgit up\b0\par\par\uc2 1,206 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2013\par 02:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Profit-taking weighs on baht after 1997 high\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not been spotted yet - traders\par \par \uc2 * Thai importers put pressure on baht\par \par \uc2 * Taiwan dlr up on exporters; ringgit higher after Fed\par \par \uc2 (Adds text, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Jongwoo Cheon\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, March 21 (Reuters) - The Thai baht slid on Thursday as caution over \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  prompted investors to book profits after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened in the previous session to levels last seen before the 1997 Asian financial crisis on sustained inflows.\par \par \uc2 The baht lost as much as 0.5 percent to 29.22 per dollar, underperforming other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Some regional units such as the Taiwan dollar and the Malaysian ringgit edged higher.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit 29.07, its strongest since 1997, according to Thomson Reuters data, as foreign investors poured into Thai bonds.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not been spotted buying dollars, but local importers bought the greenback on dips for payments, traders said.\par \par \uc2 "The market is cautious and watching if there is BOT (\uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a foreign bank trader, adding the baht may weaken to 29.24 on more dollar-short covering.\par \par \uc2 Technically, the baht is seen excessively bought with dollar/baht's 14-day relative strength index at 25.3, well below the threshold 30. The index has stayed below that level since March 15, indicating the pair has been oversold.\par \par \uc2 Late on Wednesday, BOT Governor Prasarn Trairatvorakul, who has argued before that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise was in line with economic fundamentals and with the trend in other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said it was "a bit too much and fast".\par \par \uc2 Traders and analysts suspect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the market tries to take the baht below 29.00 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The baht has been the best performing emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far this year with a 4.8 percent gain against the dollar, Thomson Reuters data showed.\par \par \uc2 The appreciation came as most of its Asian peers stayed under pressure, as a weakening yen hurt the export competitiveness of other Asian countries, especially South Korea.\par \par \uc2 Thai authorities may take steps to forestall further advances by the baht as it could hinder exports, which account for some 75 percent of gross domestic product, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 "Though outright pure \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is rather unlikely. We'd be more likely to see macro prudential measures in an effort to restrain foreign portfolio inflows," said Sacha Tihanyi, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist for Scotiabank in Hong Kong.\par \par \uc2 Still, some analysts said a firmer baht may not hit exports as hard as feared unless the global economy falters again.\par \par \uc2 Earlier, a preliminary private survey showed growth in China's vast manufacturing sector picked up in March after dipping over the Lunar New Year holiday, pointing towards solid but not spectacular first-quarter growth.\par \par \uc2 That came as the U.S. economy continued to show signs of a recovery.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  competitiveness is only one part of product competitiveness. Demand is the bigger driver, and with the U.S. economy recovering, as well as China, and emerging market demand still strong, it should still be positive for Thai exports," said \uc2 BNP Paribas\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Thio Chin Loo in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 Investors were also seeking to buy the baht on dips as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to see more capital inflows from investors seeking higher yields, traders and analysts said.\par \par \uc2 The country is also attracting more foreign direct investments and overseas money for domestic infrastructure projects, they added.\par \par \uc2 Japanese manufacturers such as car makers are stepping up investment in Thailand taking advantage of Tokyo's monetary policy easing.\par \par \uc2 "I would sell dollar/baht at 29.30 if there is no talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , because today's movement is just profit taking coupled with demand from importers, but the longer-term picture of the baht has not changed," said a Thai bank trader.\par \par \uc2 "As long as balance of payment and current account of the country still look good and there are also large investment projects by government, these are positive factors that attract offshore funds."\par \par \uc2 RINGGIT\par \par \uc2 The ringgit gained in thin trading as investors cut dollar-long positions on the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 's decision to keep its present policy stance.\par \par \uc2 The Fed kept its aggressive policy stimulus despite improvements in the U.S. economy, pointing to still-high unemployment, fiscal headwinds out of Washington and risks from abroad.\par \par \uc2 Fed Chairman \uc2 Ben Bernanke\uc2  said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might slow the pace of its bond buying but only after the labour market showed sustained improvement over a number of months.\par \par \uc2 But investors hesitated to chase the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , given sustained worries about wrangling over a bailout plan for Cyprus.\par \par \uc2 "The market has been long dollar versus ringgit. But the euro zone trouble is just causing the market to yo-yo," said a Malaysian bank trader in Kuala Lumpur.\par \par \uc2 TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar edged higher from Wednesday's domestic close of 29.845 as exporters bought it around 29.800 to the U.S. dollar, traders said.\par \par \uc2 But local interbank speculators and foreign financial institutions were lined up to sell the island's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on rallies.\par \par \uc2 Those players expected the Taiwan dollar to weaken in coming weeks, given its outperformance against some other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Asian competitors in export markets.\par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar has lost 2.2 percent to the greenback so far this year, while the South Korean won has fallen 4.0 percent and the Japanese yen has depreciated 9.3 percent, according to Thomson Reuters data.\par \par \uc2 Investors are also wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to maintain price competitiveness in overseas markets.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to push down the Taiwan dollar to close at 29.845 as usual, traders said.\par \par \uc2 In the prior session, the Taiwan dollar traded between 29.760 and 29.800 before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 Change on the day at 0640 GMT\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        95.69          96.01       +0.33\par  Sing dlr        1.2511         1.2515       +0.03\par  Taiwan dlr      29.801         29.845       +0.15\par  Korean won     1115.60        1116.10       +0.04\par  Baht             29.21          29.08       -0.45\par  Peso             40.75          40.73       -0.04\par  Rupiah         9728.00        9720.00       -0.08\par  Rupee            54.28          54.36       +0.16\par  Ringgit         3.1190         3.1225       +0.11\par  Yuan            6.2128         6.2118       -0.02\par  Change so far in 2013\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        95.69          86.79       -9.30\par  Sing dlr        1.2511         1.2219       -2.33\par  Taiwan dlr      29.801         29.136       -2.23\par  Korean won     1115.60        1070.60       -4.03\par  Baht             29.21          30.61       +4.79\par  Peso             40.75          41.05       +0.75\par  Rupiah         9728.00        9630.00       -1.01\par  Rupee            54.28          54.99       +1.32\par  Ringgit         3.1190         3.0580       -1.96\par  Yuan            6.2128         6.2303       +0.28\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Additional reporting by Miao-jung Lin in TAIPEI; Editing by Jacqueline Wong)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 1) | ABX | ABN | D | E | RBN | IF | J | M | PHD | SI | SNI | SNS | Z | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130324e93l0000k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
