\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Thai finmin wants weaker baht, lower interest rates\b0\par\par\uc2 697 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2013\par 09:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Says c.bank should take action on baht rise\par \par \uc2 * Repeats that he wants no special baht measures\par \par \uc2 (Adds detail, quotes)\par \par \uc2 By Kitiphong Thaichareon and Jongwoo Cheon\par \par \uc2 BANGKOK/SINGAPORE, March 21 (Reuters) - Thailand's finance minister said on Thursday both the baht and interest rates should be lower, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a 16-year high, threatening the export-driven economy, but he repeated there would be no capital controls to curb inflows.\par \par \uc2 Thailand is one of several Asian countries struggling to contain upward pressure on their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as investors laden with funds in the wake of quantitative easing (QE) moves by major central banks have poured money into high yield markets.\par \par \uc2 This year, the baht has been the best performing emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , strengthening 4.8 percent against the dollar, Thomson Reuters data showed.\par \par \uc2 "I want to see the baht weaker and the policy interest rate lower," Kittirat Na Ranong told a seminar. He has repeatedly called for a cut in rates to deter "hot money" but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , worried about fast credit growth and the potential for higher inflation, has resisted.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the baht hit 29.07, its strongest since 1997, according to Thomson Reuters data, as foreign investors poured into Thai bonds.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, it dipped as much as 0.5 percent to 29.22 per dollar, underperforming other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as caution over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  prompted investors to book profits.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOT) has not been spotted buying dollars, but local importers bought the greenback on dips for payments, traders said.\par \par \uc2 Kittirat spoke twice publicly about the baht on Thursday. In his earlier remarks, the finance minister said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should take action before the baht's strength bites, although in response to a reporter's question, he said he did not believe the baht would strengthen to 27 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Thailand has been attracting more foreign direct investments and inflows for domestic infrastructure projects.\par \par \uc2 The country has dealt carefully with inflows following a case in late 2006 when it imposed tough capital controls that made Thai shares plunge. In recent years, authorities have focused more on encouraging outflows.\par \par \uc2 NO SURPRISE MEASURE\par \par \uc2 Late on Wednesday, BOT Governor Prasarn Trairatvorakul, who has argued before that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise was in line with economic fundamentals and with the trend in other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said it was "a bit too much and fast".\par \par \uc2 Thai authorities may take steps to forestall further advances by the baht as its strengthening could hinder exports, which account for some 75 percent of gross domestic product, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 "Though outright pure \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is rather unlikely, we'd be more likely to see macro prudential measures in an effort to restrain foreign portfolio inflows," said Sacha Tihanyi, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist for Scotiabank in Hong Kong.\par \par \uc2 Traders and analysts suspect the BOT could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the market tries to take the baht below 29.00 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Early on Thursday, Kittirat told reporters: "People in charge (of the baht) should take action before the baht affects employment, exports and tourism."\par \par \uc2 "Temporary measures, if introduced, will hurt confidence. So I can confirm that there will be no measure that surprises the market... It should be accepted means, such as monetary measures," he added.\par \par \uc2 Kittirat has said lower interest rates would not lead to bubbles but economists have raised concerns about the rapid rise in stock prices and property.\par \par \uc2 Despite the political pressure, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy committee left the policy rate unchanged at 2.75 percent on Feb. 20, citing strong credit growth and slightly higher inflationary pressure..\par \par \uc2 Prasarn has repeatedly said that interest rates were not the only factor, or even the main factor, attracting inflows and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's main duty is to ensure economic stability.\par \par \uc2 Economists expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hold fire for some months as the economy is growing well and inflation is contained. Its next policy review is on April 3.\par \par \uc2 (Writing by Orathai Sriring; Editing by Alan Raybould and Richard Borsuk)\par \par \uc2 THAILAND-ECONOMY/BAHT  (UPDATE 2, PIX) | ABX | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | SI | RNP | DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130321e93l000d1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
