\par\par \b \uc2 ASIA DAILY  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  OUTLOOK - Asia\b0\par\par\uc2 1,657 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2013\par 01:51\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE--Following are expected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par            Immediate Range   Larger Range \par  \par    USD/CNY 6.2161-6.2245     6.2087-6.2322 \par    USD/TWD 29.745-29.900     29.500-30.000 \par    USD/KRW  1,110-1,117.2     1,100-1,120 \par    USD/SGD 1.2500-1.2542     1.2447-1.2600 \par    USD/MYR 3.1200-3.1300     3.1070-3.1500 \par    USD/THB  29.20-29.42       29.10-29.50 \par    USD/PHP  40.67-40.71       40.55-40.80 \par    USD/IDR  9,700-9,730       9,685-9,800 \par    USD/INR  54.13-54.56       54.00-55.00 \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY -- upside bias. The market is expecting a higher PBOC fixing owing to the leap in the WSJ Dollar Index following EUR/USD's tanking overnight. While the risk aversion that is building may not affect the yuan directly, there is no doubt that the pull of the broadly stronger dollar will create at least a slight upside effect in USD/CNY. Spot USD/CNY may edge higher toward the daily Ichimoku Cloud at 6.2254 before finding stiffer resistance. The changeover in leadership in China will be a backdrop for more yuan appreciation, especially after a PBOC advisor said Tuesday that there is no rush to tighten policy since the CPI will likely drift back down in March. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is likely at 6.2245 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), then at 6.2254 (Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone), before 6.2322 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate support for USD/CNY is at 6.2161 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 6.2087 (base of Bollinger downtrend channel), before 6.2000 (major psychological support).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD -- upside bias. Another leg higher looks likely for USD/TWD now that the WSJ Dollar Index has surged higher once more. The Cyprus parliament's rejection of the bank bailout proposal is hurting risk appetite as investors fathom what it could mean for other indebted peripheral European countries, such as Italy. The dive in EUR/USD overnight due to this threat is boosting the greenback higher across the board and could thus send USD/TWD to the 30.000 mark soon. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is likely at 29.900 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud top and weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 30.000 (psychological resistance), before 30.040 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate support is at 29.750 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 29.500 (psychological support), before 29.460 (20-day Bollinger mid).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW -- upside bias. USD/KRW gaps up sharply, in reaction to the Cypriot parliament rejecting the proposed bank bailout, to open at 1,115.5 after a Tuesday closing of 1,111.6. This may have caught many short-USD positions off guard and could therefore result in short-covering that might pressure USD/KRW up toward 1,120. Many moderate-thinking investors had been hoping that the Cyprus parliament would pass the plan. Now, the risk-off movement may hit full swing as the possibility that Cyprus leaves the euro is becoming more real. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 1,117.2 (Monday's high), before 1,120 (psychological barrier). Immediate support is at 1,110 (psychological support), then at 1,1103 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1,100 (major psychological support).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD -- upside bias. USD/SGD is well on its way toward the 1.2550-1.2560 triple-top region, propelled by the greenback's broad rally and guided higher by the daily Bollinger uptrend channel. A rejection of the Cyprus bank bailout is likely to have deeper repercussions on the rest of Europe and therefore the euro, and may push the WSJ Dollar Index even higher. The likelihood of USD/SGD rallying depends on whether the risk aversion in Europe spreads to global stock markets, which could trigger a widespread flight to safety; at the moment, it appears to be contained. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate resistance is at 1.2542 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1.2600 (psychological resistance). Immediate support is at 1.2500 (psychological support), then at 1.2494 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1.2447 (20-day Bollinger mid support).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR -- upside bias. USD/MYR has solidified its stance within the Bollinger uptrend channel, thanks to the burst of USD strength overnight. The greenback may soon rally past Monday's peak of 3.1390, and head for the psychological barrier at 3.1500 as risk aversion comes to a boil. Malaysia Prime Minister Najib made a scheduled television appearance late Tuesday, priming the public for the upcoming election by reiterating the government's achievements thus far; but no polling date has been mentioned yet. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 3.1300 (psychological resistance), then at 3.1350 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.1500 (psychological resistance). Immediate support is at 3.1200 (psychological support and base of Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 3.1070 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 3.1000 (major psychological support).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB -- downside bias. USD/THB is nearing its 5-year low of 29.20 (Jan 2008) as the baht continues to strengthen on the back of inflows for the sale of GE'S stake in Bank Ayudhya, as well as for the upcoming BTS initial public offering, said to be worth $2.1 billion. The baht has been so far unaffected by developments in Europe that have shaken global investor confidence. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Tuesday that there is no need for concern over its recent strength, which could mean that USD/THB may fall further, since the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  anytime soon. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 29.20 (Jan 2008 low), then at 29.10 (July 2007 low), before 29.00 (major psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 29.42 (lower Bollinger band standard deviation 2), then at 29.50 (psychological resistance), before 29.60 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP -- consolidation. USD/PHP is showing signs of consolidation between the 20-day Bollinger mid of 40.67 and the daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone that overhangs at 40.71. Risk aversion may drive the pair slightly higher as the dollar becomes a safe haven, but the additional resistance level nearby at 40.73, which is the Bollinger uptrend channel, may help to keep a lid on USD/PHP. If, however, the latter level is breached on a daily closing basis, there might be a stronger upside reaction for the dollar. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 40.71 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance), then at 40.73 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 40.80 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate support is at 40.67 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 40.61 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 40.55 (bottom of daily Bollinger downtrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR -- upside bias. More room has appeared to the topside in USD/IDR as the pair now is clearly above the Ichimoku Cloud support zone and heading for the top of the Bollinger uptrend channel at 9,730. Although the rupiah has not shown much reaction to the recent risk-off move in the high-beta \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders could be getting ready for panic dollar buying if the euro collapses further -- a likely possibility given Cyprus' rejection of the bank bailout proposal. The Cyprus deal breakdown has ramifications for other indebt euro-zone countries; contagion to Greece or Italy would be disastrous. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 9,730 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 9,800 (psychological resistance). Immediate support is at 9,700 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel and psychological support), then at 9,685 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support), before 9,675 (base of Ichimoku Cloud support).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR -- consolidation with upside bias. The rupee may be in for more pain as the dollar/rupee pair may soon enter the Bollinger uptrend channel at 54.56 and then head for the psychological resistance at 55.00. The RBI on Tuesday cut by 25 bps its repo and reverse-repo rates -- the benchmark borrowing costs for commercial banks -- which was expected, though this easing was overshadowed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  saying that there is limited room for further easing. But the real kicker that hit the rupee hard was when the DMK political party withdrew from the ruling government coalition, citing lack of support for its views on Sri Lanka. USD/INR surged from 54.02 to end the day much higher at 54.49, well above the Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone, thus creating a bullish bias for the dollar/rupee pair. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 54.56 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 55.00 (psychological resistance), before 55.05 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate support is at 54.13 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support zone), then at 54.06 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 54.00 (psychological support).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew 