\par\par \b \uc2 Thai baht near 28-mth high on offshore funds;  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  talk caps\b0\par\par\uc2 375 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2013\par 06:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, March 15 (Reuters) - The Thai baht rose on Friday to hover around a 28-month high on continued demand from offshore funds, but speculation of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb its rise capped the upside, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The baht gained 0.3 percent to 29.55 per dollar as of 0513 GMT after hitting 29.54, according to Thomson Reuters data. The session high matched Tuesday's peak, the strongest mark since November 2010.\par \par \uc2 Traders said they have spotted \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bids for the dollar around its lows while importers also bought the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But some market players dismissed the suggestion that the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the day.\par \par \uc2 Investors were generally looking to buy the baht given the continued foreign-fund inflows, traders said.\par \par \uc2 "They are \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth the fall in dollar/baht. But the inflows are persistent and the baht is very strong. Nothing can shake it," said a foreign bank trader, expecting more offshore inflows linked to the country's infrastructure projects.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently when the baht has gone past 29.60 per dollar due to concerns the country's export competitiveness will be eroded, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The baht has been the best performing emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far this year with a 3.6 percent appreciation against the dollar, Thomson Reuters data showed, helped by offshore fund inflows to the country's stocks and bonds.\par \par \uc2 Bullish positions in the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  increased in the last two week, a Reuters poll showed on late Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Some investors locked in profits as the baht was considered to be in overbought territory. The dollar/baht's 14-day relative strength index stood at 29.8, lower than the 30-threshold, indicating the pair is near oversold territory.\par \par \uc2 Still, traders preferred to buy the local unit on dips.\par \par \uc2 A local trader said he doubted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  around the current levels, adding the authorities would probably step in when the baht strengthens further to 29.50.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Jongwoo Cheon; Editing by Shri Navaratnam)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-THAILAND-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 / | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130315e93f0006h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
