\par\par \b \uc2 ASIA DAILY  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  OUTLOOK - Asia\b0\par\par\uc2 1,241 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Januar 2013\par 01:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE--Following are expected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range    Larger Range \par  \par USD/CNY   6.2128-6.2207      6.2000-6.2285 \par USD/TWD   29.040-29.080      29.000-29.110 \par USD/KRW   1,063-1,068.6      1,060-1,070 \par USD/SGD   1.2249-1.2376      1.2213-1.2300 \par USD/MYR   -                  - \par USD/THB   29.62-29.84        29.50-30.00 \par USD/PHP   40.55-40.75        40.50-40.94 \par USD/IDR   -                  - \par USD/INR   53.37-54.00        53.00-54.19 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis - Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY -- consolidation. Markets will be eagerly awaiting the January HSBC China Flash Manufacturing PMI, out at 0145 GMT. A strong print could give the stock market some impetus to trade higher, which could help temper the slightly bearish risk sentiment spilling over from disappointment with South Korea's 4Q GDP data. The PBOC central parity rate might hover around Wednesday's fix of 6.2762, given the slight movement in the WSJ dollar index. USD/CNY may thus continue to consolidate with a mid-term bearish bias within the Bollinger downtrend channel. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 6.2128 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 6.2100 (psychological support), before 6.2000 (major psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 6.2207 (ceiling of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 6.2285 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 6.2364 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD -- consolidation. More sideways price action in USD/TWD is likely, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to keep a firm lid on the Taiwan dollar around 28.950. The pair can be expected to stay trapped within a narrow range of 28.930-29.110, capped by the Ichimoku Cloud resistance and supported by suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that is keeping USD/TWD above the psychological level of 29.000. Volatility is likely to remain low given the pair's resistance to both sides of the present range. Dow Jones technical analysis shows initial support is at 29.040 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 29.000 (psychological support), before 28.930 (Jan. 14 low). Immediate resistance is at 29.080 (ceiling of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 29.110 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance), before 29.120 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW -- upside bias. USD/KRW may add to gains this week, after the South Korea's Q4 GDP data failed to meet expectations, expanding just 0.4% versus a consensus of 0.5%. The greenback is displaying bullish tendencies against the won after USD/KRW closed above the 20-day Bollinger mid at 1,063 on Wednesday. The next target for the pair could be the Bollinger uptrend channel. Entry into the channel, which is contingent on a daily close above 1,068.6, could unlock more upside potential. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,063 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 1,060 (psychological support), before 1,057 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1,068.6 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1,070 (psychological resistance), before 1,074 (ceiling of Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD -- mild upside bias. USD/SGD appears to be grinding its way higher, but the going is expected to be slow as the pair once again failed to enter the Bollinger uptrend channel. Momentum thus looks weak, though the upside bias persists as long as USD/SGD stays above the 20-day Bollinger mid at 1.2252. A close under this level, which could happen on a strong January HSBC China flash PMI due later, might see a further downside break toward the Ichimoku Cloud support at 1.2229. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2252 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 1.2229 (Ichimoku Cloud support), before 1.2212 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud support zone). Immediate resistance is at 1.2278 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2300 (psychological barrier), before 1.2331 (Jan. 7 high).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR -- closed for Birthday of Prophet Muhammad.\par \par \uc2 USD/THB -- consolidation. USD/THB is finally showing some resilience to the selling pressure that has been weighing on the pair since it broke the psychological barrier of 30.00. The baht is holding steady near 29.75, thanks to several rounds of verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor. USD/THB is starting to form a base here and could possibly rally if punters begin to take back their short-USD positions once they are convinced that the BOT won't let the baht gain much more. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 29.62 (Jan. 21 low), then at 29.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 29.80 (Bollinger band standard deviation 2), then at 30.00 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP -- consolidation. USD/PHP might see-saw within its intraweek range of 40.59-40.75 for now, lacking strong signals in either direction. The \uc2 Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  monetary policy meeting today is unlikely to result in any rate adjustments, say analysts. Thus, the peso could be driven by regional forces instead, which could mean that USD/PHP rises toward the top of its recent range, possibly testing the ceiling of the daily Bollinger downtrend channel which currently caps at 40.75. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 40.55 (bottom of Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 40.50 (psychological support and base of weekly Bollinger downtrend channel), before 40.25 (five-year low). Immediate resistance is at 40.75 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 40.94 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 41.00 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR -- closed for Birthday of Prophet Muhammad.\par \par \uc2 USD/INR -- consolidation with downside bias. USD/INR still looks biased lower after the pair closed under the Ichimoku Cloud again, despite a brief rally Wednesday on the back of the RBI removing a rule that required exporters to convert at least half of their foreign earnings into rupees -- which in effect removes a significant source of dollar liquidity from the market. USD/INR could be headed for the psychological barrier at 53.00 next, though a holiday on Friday could keep risk appetite at bay, and hence force the rupee into a narrow trading range. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 53.37 (Tuesday's low), then at 53.00 (psychological barrier). Immediate resistance is at 54.00 (psychological barrier), then at 54.19 (Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone and ceiling of daily Bollinger downtrend channel).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 Original Email Message: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://SINNWSENEWSP1.newswires.dowjones.net/Enewsmails/Links.aspx?Ac=22&ID=20130124-08212682-0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://SINNWSENEWSP1.newswires.dowjones.net/Enewsmails/Links.aspx?Ac=22&ID=20130124-08212682-0}}}\uc2  [ 24-01-13 0039GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1136   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130124e91o0000j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
