\par\par \b \uc2 ASIA DAILY  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  OUTLOOK - Asia\b0\par\par\uc2 1,397 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Januar 2013\par 01:38\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE--Following are expected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range    Larger Range \par  \par USD/CNY   6.2134-6.2211      6.2000-6.2288 \par USD/TWD   29.040-29.080      29.000-29.100 \par USD/KRW   1,060-1,063        1,057-1,070 \par USD/SGD   1.2249-1.2376      1.2213-1.2300 \par USD/MYR   3.0345-3.0500      3.0180-3.0550 \par USD/THB   29.62-29.84        29.50-30.00 \par USD/PHP   40.57-40.76        40.50-40.95 \par USD/IDR   9,700-9,800        9,620-9,900 \par USD/INR   53.37-53.74        53.00-54.00 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis - Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY -- downside bias. The overnight fall in the WSJ dollar index to 70.705 from nearly 71.000 may indicate that the PBOC USD/CNY central parity rate will be lower today. A likely range for the fix could be between 6.2700-6.2750. A lower fixing would guide spot USD/CNY back down towards the bottom of the Bollinger downtrend channel at 6.2134. Chinese stocks could add to gains as the SSEC uptrend line continues to lead the index higher toward the May 2012 high of 2,453.7. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 6.2134 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 6.2100 (psychological support), before 6.2000 (major psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 6.2211 (ceiling of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 6.2288 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 6.2365 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD -- consolidation. More sideways price action in USD/TWD is likely, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to keep the Taiwan dollar weak in order to support its exporters. The pair can be expected to stay trapped within a narrow range of 28.930-29.100, capped by the Ichimoku Cloud resistance and supported by suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that is keeping USD/TWD above the psychological level of 29.000. Volatility is likely to remain low given the resilience of both sides of the present range. Dow Jones technical analysis shows initial support is at 29.040 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 29.000 (psychological support), before 28.930 (Jan. 14 low). Immediate resistance is at 29.080 (ceiling of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 29.100 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance), before 29.120 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW -- downside bias. USD/KRW 's sharp turnaround toward the end of Tuesday has negated the likelihood of a rally, after the pair reversed lower and closed under the 20-day Bollinger mid support at 1,063. Now it appears more likely that USD/KRW will be sold lower, toward the psychological support at 1,060 and possibly back into the Bollinger downtrend channel that begins at 1,057. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,060 (psychological support), then at 1,057 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1,051 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1,063 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), then at 1,070 (psychological resistance and Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD -- mild upside bias. USD/SGD could ease slightly Wednesday but the upside bias remains, if slightly weaker, as long as the pair stays above the 20-day Bollinger mid support at 1.2249. The greenback came off its Tuesday highs as USD/JPY tanked and EUR/USD recovered, weighing on the dollar index. A consolidation toward the Bollinger mid support line may be necessary before USD/SGD explores more upside. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2249 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 1.2232 (Ichimoku Cloud support), before 1.2213 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud support zone). Immediate resistance is at 1.2276 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2300 (psychological barrier), before 1.2331 (Jan. 7 high).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR -- consolidation with upside bias. USD/MYR is displaying bullish tendencies on the charts, but the pair could consolidate first, as the USD eases broadly following USD/JPY's drop and EUR/USD's recovery. With price action currently above the 20-day Bollinger mid of 3.0345, another leg higher appears more likely -- unless the pair ends Wednesday under the Bollinger mid. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.0345 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 3.0300 (psychological support), before 3.0180 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is 3.0500 (psychological resistance and Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.0550 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB -- consolidation. Verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor may help to prop USD/THB up near 29.70. The governor on Tuesday said that "recent uncertainties in the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market warrant special monitoring," and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has the tools to curb the baht's rise if necessary. Hence, USD/THB may start to form a base here and could possibly rally if punters begin to take back their short-USD positions once they are convinced that the BOT won't let the baht gain much more. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 29.62 (Jan. 21 low), then at 29.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 29.84 (Bollinger band standard deviation 2), then at 30.00 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP -- downside bias. USD/PHP may now have a slightly bearish bias after the pair dropped back under the confirmation line of the double-bottom formation that was showing up Tuesday. Now, the greenback may slide back down toward the suspected BSP \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level near 40.50-40.55. Weighing the dollar down is weakness in USD/JPY, which is beginning to show signs of a further pullback to come. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 40.57 (bottom of Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 40.50 (psychological support and base of weekly Bollinger downtrend channel), before 40.25 (five-year low). Immediate resistance is at 40.76 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 40.95 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 41.00 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR -- downside bias. USD/IDR trades with a softer tone as the dollar slides across the board, helping to bring the grey market price of dollars, currently at 9,740, closer to the official spot market price of around 9,620. Traders and hedge funds are catching on to this correction move in USD/IDR, particularly looking for further convergence of the grey market prices and the official spot market price. USD/IDR is thus likely to trade lower over the course of the week. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is now at 9,700 (psychological support), before 9,620 (official spot level). Immediate resistance is at 9,800 (psychological resistance), then at 9,900 (psychological barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR -- consolidation with downside bias. USD/INR could consolidate, judging by the dollar's sharp recovery towards the close of the market on Tuesday. The pair ended just below the Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone, which is a bearish sign, yet the formation of a long-tailed doji candlestick suggests that buying interest is strong near 53.40, and hence consolidation may be likely for now. But as long as USD/INR stays under the Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone, the downside is still more likely in the mid-term. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 53.37 (Tuesday's low), then at 53.00 (psychological barrier). Immediate resistance is at 53.74 (Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone), then at 54.00 (psychological barrier), then at 54.24 (ceiling of daily Bollinger downtrend channel).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.) [ 23-01-13 0038GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1136   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130123e91n0000m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
