\par\par \b \uc2 ASIA DAILY  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  OUTLOOK - Asia\b0\par\par\uc2 1,371 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Januar 2013\par 01:41\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--Following are expected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range    Larger Range \par  \par USD/CNY   6.2136-6.2215      6.2000-6.2295 \par USD/TWD   29.050-29.080      29.000-29.100 \par USD/KRW   1,058-1,065        1,051-1,070 \par USD/SGD   1.2276-1.2300      1.2249-1.2331 \par USD/MYR   3.0300-3.0350      3.0180-3.0500 \par USD/THB   29.62-29.91        29.50-30.00 \par USD/PHP   40.64-40.77        40.50-40.96 \par USD/IDR   9,700-9,800        9,620-9,900 \par USD/INR   53.62-53.92        53.00-54.00 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis - Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY -- consolidation. The WSJ dollar index eased slightly overnight, which might indicate a stable or slightly lower USD/CNY fixing today. The yuan could hence gain a little, guided lower by the likely lower PBOC central parity rate, and might slip lower to the bottom of the Bollinger downtrend channel at 6.2136. The CNY NDF premium curve has compressed significantly, with the one-year premium nearly par to the one-month premium, which could mean that most of the appreciation for the yuan may have been priced in already. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 6.2136 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 6.2100 (psychological support), before 6.2000 (major psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 6.2215 (ceiling of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 6.2295 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 6.2372 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD -- consolidation. USD/TWD is likely to stay trapped within a narrow range of 28.930-29.100, capped by the Ichimoku Cloud resistance and supported by Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which continues to prop up the pair around the end of each day, keeping USD/TWD above the psychological level of 29.000. Volatility is likely to remain low given the pair's resilience to both sides of the present range. Dow Jones technical analysis shows initial support is at 29.050 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 29.000 (psychological support), before 28.930 (Jan. 14 low). Immediate resistance is at 29.080 (ceiling of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 29.100 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance), before 29.120 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW -- possible upside bias. USD/KRW's late rally Monday may ease slightly as exporters could take the chance to sell dollars at these elevated levels. The rally into Monday's close nearly broke the 20-day Bollinger mid resistance at 1,064, which could have led to more short-covering today. If the pair manages a daily close above the Bollinger mid, the technical bias for a rally increases. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,058 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1,051 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1,050 (psychological support level and suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level). Immediate resistance is at 1,065 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), then at 1,070 (psychological resistance and Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD -- upside bias. USD/SGD is displaying bullish technical signals as the pair enters the daily Bollinger uptrend channel. It looks like USD/SGD is on the path toward the psychological barrier at 1.2400, a level last seen in September. The Bollinger uptrend channel is supporting the pair at 1.2276. A slightly softer tone in EUR/USD may be helping to push the USD index higher, thus giving USD/SGD a boost as well. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2276 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2249 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 1.2213 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud support zone). Immediate resistance is at 1.2300 (psychological barrier), then at 1.2304 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1.2331 (Jan. 7 high).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR -- consolidation with upside bias. USD/MYR has rocketed out of the Bollinger downtrend channel but may have found a temporary ceiling at the 20-day Bollinger mid at 3.0350. The pair has inched higher since the open and stabilized, though the declining EUR/USD could well send the greenback higher again and propel USD/MYR past this key resistance and into bullish territory. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.0300 (psychological support), then at 3.0180 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 3.0000 (major psychological support). Immediate resistance is 3.0350 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), before 3.0500 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB -- consolidation with upside bias. Suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been propping USD/THB up near 29.70 recently, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may soon get some help from the rallying USD. As regional USD/Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs rise into bullish territory, USD/THB may get dragged higher in sync, possibly heading toward the Bollinger standard deviation 2 line at 29.91; beyond that mark is the psychological barrier of 30.00. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 29.62 (Jan. 21 low), then at 29.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 29.91 (Bollinger band standard deviation 2), then at 30.00 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP -- upside bias. USD/PHP may rally higher after confirmation of a double-bottom formation -- the pair rallied past the confirmation line at 40.64 on Monday, and could next test the top of the Bollinger downtrend channel at 40.77. A breakout of the Bollinger downtrend channel could be additionally bullish for USD/PHP, suggesting a return to the Bollinger mid at 40.96 could be possible. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 40.64 (double bottom confirmation line), then at 40.50 (psychological support and base of weekly Bollinger downtrend channel), before 40.25 (five-year low). Immediate resistance is at 40.77 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 40.96 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 41.00 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR -- consolidation. USD/IDR dropped sharply Monday on keen selling by hedge funds late in the day, says an NDF dealer. The pair dropped below the psychological level of 9,800 in the grey market. The implied spot level (via the NDF market) is currently around 9,760, which means the grey market is starting to converge with the official spot market, which trades around 9,620. The downside momentum in USD/IDR, however, could be tempered by the overall biddish tone in USD/Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is now at 9,700 (psychological support), before 9,620 (official spot level). Immediate resistance is at 9,800 (psychological resistance), then at 9,900 (psychological barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR -- consolidation. USD/INR may have found a base at the bottom of the Ichimoku Cloud base at 53.62. This could mean the downside move could slow, and possibly even retrace a little higher as the greenback rallies broadly against Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Unless USD/INR manages a daily close under the Cloud and therefore regains downside momentum, the pair may stall for now. USD/INR could trade in a range of 53.62-54.00 Tuesday. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 53.62 (base of Ichimoku Cloud), then at 53.00 (psychological barrier). Immediate resistance is at 53.92 (Bollinger band standard deviation 2), then at 54.00 (psychological barrier), then at 54.33 (ceiling of daily Bollinger downtrend channel).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.) [ 22-01-13 0041GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1136   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130122e91m0000k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
