\par\par \b \uc2 REFILE-EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Taiwan dlr, won lead slight Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  gains on exporters\b0\par\par\uc2 929 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 2012\par 09:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Deletes extraneous words from second paragraph)\par \par \uc2 * Taiwan dlr up 0.5 pct on exporters month-end demand\par \par \uc2 * South Korean exporters support won\par \par \uc2 * Philippine peso largely ignores trade data\par \par \uc2 By Jongwoo Cheon\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Sept 25 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose slightly on Tuesday with the South Korean won and the Taiwan dollar gaining from exporter demand, with analysts noting recent policy stimulus by major central banks could help regional units offset a sluggish global economy.\par \par \uc2 The Philippine peso edged higher as traders showed muted reaction to a dip in the country's imports in July.\par \par \uc2 Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' appreciation came even as regional stocks edged lower amid worries that a slowing global economy will keep biting into Asia's exports, the area's main growth engine.\par \par \uc2 "The outlook for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains bright as major central banks decided to prevent downside risks on the economy with unlimited bond-buying. The liquidity pump will give Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  room to rise more," said Yuna Park, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and bond analyst at \uc2 Dongbu Securities\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The China economy is also expected to improve if funds from the U.S. and the Europe come to Asia," said Park, adding the ringgit, the Thai baht and the Singapore dollar may lead the gains.\par \par \uc2 Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities are likely to try to slow down their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains, but they would not resist a global trend, she said.\par \par \uc2 Most emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have gained so far this month as the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  and the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  eased monetary policies to spur their economy, while European policy makers took measures to tackle the euro zone's debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 Still, regional units were not free from worries about a lukewarm global economy, which analysts said increased chances of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  across the region.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's exports in August fell 6.95 percent from a year ago, worse than expected. Germany's business confidence in September slid for a fifth consecutive month and \uc2 Caterpillar Inc\uc2 ., the world's largest maker of earth-moving equipment, cut its earnings forecast.\par \par \uc2 The euro zone's debt crisis is still far from over with Spain staying in focus. Its government bond yields rose on concerns that the country is dragging its feet in requesting the international bailout that most market participants expect.\par \par \uc2 The worries have prompted investors to book profits from emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  since last week.\par \par \uc2 TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar advanced as some domestic exporters bought for month-end settlements around 29.340-29.350 to the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has barely been spotted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although it may step into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market around the last minutes of domestic trading to weaken the closing price, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 Still, local importers also bought U.S. dollars for payments, limiting the Taiwan dollar's upside, dealers added.\par \par \uc2 WON\par \par \uc2 The won gained on demand from South Korean exporters for month-end settlements, although interbank speculators hesitated to join them on caution over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength.\par \par \uc2 Sustained worries about a slowing global economy also kept the lid on appetite for the won among interbank speculators.\par \par \uc2 "Some preferred the won, given shipbuilders' demand, but I wonder how many more dollar offers we will see here," said a senior foreign bank dealer in Seoul, adding the market is seen consolidating.\par \par \uc2 PHILIPPINE PESO\par \par \uc2 The Philippine peso edged higher with the euro holding ground, while traders showed muted reaction to a dip in the country's imports in July.\par \par \uc2 Philippine exports fell in July, for the first time in three months, on slower electronic shipments, highlighting weak demand from the country's main trading partners as a sluggish global economy bites.\par \par \uc2 The weak indicator does not necessarily mean a pressure on the peso, a foreign bank dealer in Manila said.\par \par \uc2 "The data was prior to the QE3 and it did have much of an impact as most of it was already expected," the dealer said.\par \par \uc2 "The test will be the data after QE3," he added.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 Change on the day at 0630 GMT\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        77.77          77.83       +0.08\par  Sing dlr        1.2278         1.2275       -0.02\par  Taiwan dlr      29.341         29.479       +0.47\par  Korean won     1118.80        1120.50       +0.15\par  Baht             30.94          30.95       +0.03\par  Peso      