\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: BOT: Brisk Credit Growth May Make Rate Cut Less Effective\b0\par\par\uc2 503 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 September 2012\par 09:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- Consumption and investment are growing thanks to higher wages and reconstruction\par \par \uc2 -- Won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  with baht provided movement is in line with economic fundamentals\par \par \uc2 -- Considering easing rules to promote offshore investment\par \par \uc2 (Recasts the first paragraph, and adds comments from the BOT governor plus context throughout.)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Phisanu Phromchanya \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BANGKOK--\f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  Gov. Prasarn Trairatvorakul Monday said the current brisk pace of lending growth may reduce the effectiveness of any new monetary stimulus, and that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  won't \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market provided the baht moves in line with Thailand's economic fundamentals.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 External headwind is clearly hurting exports, but private consumption and investment show healthy growth thanks primarily to higher wages and reconstruction activity in areas damaged by last year's floods, Gov. Prasarn told reporters on the sidelines of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's annual symposium.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "At a time when finance institutions are registering robust [on-year] credit growth of around 15% to 16% [in August] and are continuing to compete for deposits, any policy rate cut may not be effective" in stimulating the economy, Gov. Prasarn said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The BOT's Monetary Policy Committee at its latest review meeting on Sept. 5 kept its policy interest rate at 3.0% for the fifth consecutive meeting, saying it is appropriate for current economic conditions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The MPC said it will be vigilant in monitoring domestic demand conditions, private credit growth and developments in the global economy, and that it is ready to take appropriate action as warranted.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Regarding \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Gov. Prasarn said the baht has been relatively stable against the U.S. dollar compared with regional peers since the U.S. Federal Reserve announced a third bond-buying program, known as quantitative easing.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar weakened to THB30.91-THB30.93 in early trade Monday from just above THB31.00 before the QE3 announcement on Sept. 13.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Funds released by the Fed's bond-buying could flow into Asia and push up the value of the baht, but the BOT will only consider \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  action when movement is distorted by unusual factors.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It is not our objective to take care of all \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  risk for the private sector, they have to manage this risk themselves...So long as the baht moves along with [\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's] economic fundamentals, we have no intention to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at all," Gov. Prasarn said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 He said offshore investment has helped offset upward pressure on the baht. During the January-August period, capital outflows amounted to around $8 billion, whereas inflows into bonds and equities reached around $10 billion, he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The BOT is considering easing rules to promote offshore investment, Gov. Prasarn said without elaborating.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's primary objective is to maintain economic stability through adjusting its policy interest rate or, for instance, through \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  or macro prudential measures. Such measures could simultaneously promote growth.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Phisanu Phromchanya at phisanu.phromchanya@dowjones.com [ 24-09-12 0728GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120924e89o000dg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
