\par\par \b \uc2 Bank Of  \highlight22\uc2 Thailand \highlight\uc2 : Have Not  \highlight22\uc2 Intervened \highlight\uc2  In  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Markets Recently\b0\par\par\uc2 115 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Mai 2012\par 08:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets recently despite the baht's rapid pace of depreciation, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Senior Director Singhachai Boonyayotin said Thursday.\par \par \uc2 He attributed the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent weakness mainly to a softer euro against the U.S. dollar, and noted the baht's movements were still in line with that of regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The BOT is closely monitoring movements in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and hasn't detected any unusual capital flows movement, said Singhachai.\par \par \uc2 -By Bangkok Bureau, Dow Jones Newswires; 662-690-4200; djnews.bangkok@dowjones.com [ 31-05-12 0659GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120531e85v000ek\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
