\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Baht to see best week in a month, Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  mostly up\b0\par\par\uc2 1,018 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2012\par 05:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Baht steady on dlr-short covering, c.bank comment\par \par \uc2 * S.Korean exporters, importers lock won in range\par \par \uc2 * Philippine peso up on euro\par \par \uc2 (Adds details, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Jongwoo Cheon\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Feb 24 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  gained on Friday on strong U.S. and German data, with the Thai baht set to enjoy its best week in nearly one month thanks to inflows including Japanese flood insurance payouts.\par \par \uc2 Investors took some profits from the regional units before the weekend, but the unit were likely to stay firm next week despite sustained concerns over rising oil prices, dealers and analysts said.\par \par \uc2 "I am positive on risk until early next week," said a senior European bank dealer in Singapore, adding he was most positive about the South Korean won and the Singapore dollar.\par \par \uc2 Emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were aided this week by China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decision last weekend to pump up liquidity to boost growth, and by the euro zone finance ministers' approval of a second bailout fund for Greece.\par \par \uc2 The regional units also gained against the yen, with the baht reaching its strongest level since August as the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stayed under pressure following the Bank of Japan's surprise policy easing on Feb. 14.\par \par \uc2 The regional units experienced some correction because of higher oil prices amid escalating tension over Iran's nuclear programme, which could further dent the fragile European economy.\par \par \uc2 But some \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were certain to report weekly gains after being buoyed by strong U.S. jobs and housing data, as well as a stronger-than-expected German business sentiment indicator.\par \par \uc2 Among the weekly winners, the baht has risen 1.4 percent against the dollar, according to Thomson Reuters data. If the Thai unit maintains the gain, that would be the largest weekly rise since the week ended on Jan 29, the data showed.\par \par \uc2 Still, many dealers question how much further emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  can rise given surging oil prices and caution over the global economic picture.\par \par \uc2 The European Commission's forecast that economic output in the euro zone would contract 0.3 percent this year, while the European Union will stagnate, could see emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  hold in recent ranges, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 "Look at the rising oil prices. Who dares to say there is no tension in the Middle East?" said a senior dealer at a Malaysian bank in Kuala Lumpur, adding that further appreciation in emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be slow.\par \par \uc2 Westpac\uc2  said in a note that the Indian rupee and Indonesian rupiah are most vulnerable among regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to higher oil prices.\par \par \uc2 BAHT\par \par \uc2 Dollar/baht recovered most of its initial losses as investors covered short positions amid caution over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Deputy Governor Suchada Kirakul said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has risen quickly recently and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is monitoring fund inflows, especially those into the bond market.\par \par \uc2 Earlier, the pair slid on expectation of inflows linked to Japanese insurance claims, but found support at 30.20, the 76.4 percent Fibonacci retracement of its July-January rises.\par \par \uc2 Some hedging flows put pressure on the pair, while insurance flows have not been seen yet, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 Still, dollar/baht may head lower again with more insurance-linked inflows, a trader said.\par \par \uc2 "The flows are continuing for some time. So I am targeting 29.80," he said.\par \par \uc2 WON\par \par \uc2 Dollar/won was confined in a tight range after gapping lower as South Korean exporters and importers engaged in a battle around mid-1,120, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 The pair moved between 1,124.0 and 1,125.9 during the local trade after opening at 1,124.3.\par \par \uc2 "Both bids and offers from corporates are pretty strong and there is no room for interbank players to move. The euro holds a key, but I don't think dollar/won can break through support at 1,120, even though the euro rises further," said a senior foreign bank dealer in Seoul.\par \par \uc2 PHILIPPINE PESO\par \par \uc2 Dollar/Philippine peso slid on a firm euro, while its slide was limited as some speculators covered short positions before the weekend, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 But a European bank dealer in Manila expects the pair to fall next week, probably to 42.40 eventually.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 Change on the day at 0715 GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        80.59          80.00       -0.73\par  Sing dlr        1.2546         1.2540       -0.05\par  Taiwan dlr      29.554         29.596       +0.14\par  Korean won     1124.90        1129.00       +0.36\par  Baht             30.35          30.35       +0.00\par  Peso             42.70          42.78       