\par\par \b \uc2 INTERVIEW-UPDATE 1-Thai c.bank chief says FIDF debt service a non-issue\b0\par\par\uc2 816 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Februar 2012\par 11:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, quotes)\par \par \uc2 * C.bank says FIDF debt task won't interfere with monetary policy\par \par \uc2 * No inclination to weaken \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to meet debt task\par \par \uc2 * Prasarn: monetary policy normalised, already accommodative\par \par \uc2 * C.bank sees Q3 shift in balance of risk to growth/inflation\par \par \uc2 By Vidya Ranganathan and Orathai Sriring\par \par \uc2 BANGKOK, Feb 15 (Reuters) - Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will make absolutely sure that its new responsibility to service a massive 15-year-old mountain of debt dating back to the Asian financial crisis does not interfere with monetary or \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, its governor said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Having recently been tasked with servicing interest payments on the 1.14 trillion baht ($37 billion) debt, a legacy of Thailand's bailout of banks in 1997, Governor Prasarn Trairatvorakul dismisses any talk the deal will require the \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  to generate income from its management of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  or its dollar reserves.\par \par \uc2 "It will never interfere with any monetary policy decisions," Prasarn said. "There is no inclination whatsoever to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 Speaking to Reuters in an interview, Prasarn said the fragility of consumer and business sentiment posed a bigger risk to the economy, which has barely recovered from the impact of heavy flooding late last year.\par \par \uc2 Inflationary expectations were contained and policy rates were suitably loose at levels slightly below the headline inflation rate, he said.\par \par \uc2 "The path of monetary policy at the moment can be accommodative, at least to enhance the recovery, make it firmer, make it faster. It's already accommodative," Prasarn said.\par \par \uc2 "Probably the critical time will be from the middle of the year and within the third quarter. Probably we may see some shift in the balance of risks to growth and inflation," Prasarn said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  has cut rates twice since the end of November. At 3 percent, its policy rate is slightly below annual headline inflation, which was 3.38 percent in January.\par \par \uc2 Prasarn acknowledged there were risks from inflation. The implementation of a minimum wage of 300 baht a day could add 0.2 percentage point to headline inflation, he said. Another government measure to raise the floor price for rice could add 0.3 point, while a lowering of fuel subsidies could push inflation another full point higher.\par \par \uc2 But pressure on growth, particularly from slower exports, would help contain price rises until the third quarter when the economy would be performing closer to full capacity, he said.\par \par \uc2 NO FINANCING GAP\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief seemed confident this week's proposal on servicing the debt owed by the Financial Institutions Development Fund (FIDF) would leave no gaps on its balance-sheet.\par \par \uc2 By transferring the servicing burden to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the government hopes to free up cash for building flood defences.\par \par \uc2 Under the proposal, Thailand's banks would pay a levy of 0.47 percent on deposits, up from 0.4 percent currently. Most of the levy would be diverted from a deposit protection agency to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and used to service the debt.\par \par \uc2 Analysts estimate the approximately 45 billion baht that could be raised annually through the levy will fall short of the 60-65 billion interest payments on the FIDF debt.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  would either have to issue its own bonds or generate heavier profits on its $179 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, they reckon. The latter would entail letting the baht weaken substantially, or lighter \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  when it appreciates.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's calculations present a different picture, Prasarn said. There is enough cash from existing provisions in the budget, from accrued balances with the deposit protection agency, and in the form of FIDF assets to bridge the gap. In addition, the debt would be refinanced gradually at rates far lower than those in 1997, he said.\par \par \uc2 "There won't be any serious gap for us," he said.\par \par \uc2 YUAN ASSETS\par \par \uc2 Prasarn said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would increase the composition of assets denominated in the Chinese yuan this year, given China had already given it permission to buy Chinese bonds in the interbank market.\par \par \uc2 Referring to the sharp jump in the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's forward positions in baht, Prasarn said that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was aimed at evening out distortions in the swap curve spawned by the crunch in dollar funding markets globally. The \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2 's forward book jumped by more than 50 percent to $31 billion in 2011.\par \par \uc2 "We tried to stabilise and accommodate the dollar demand from the market," Prasarn said.\par \par \uc2 Prasarn said the \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  was in talks with Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a liquidity management agreement like the one it agreed with its Malayian counterpart earlier this month..\par \par \uc2 It was also looking at similar arrangements with other Asia-Pacific central banks.\par \par \uc2 ($1=30.8 baht)\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Alan Raybould)\par \par \uc2 THAILAND-ECONOMY/INTERVIEW   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120218e82f0009e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
