\par\par \b \uc2 RUBBER-Tokyo futures hit 2-week high on Thai  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  hope\b0\par\par\uc2 506 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 2012\par 02:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Jan 12 (Reuters) - Tokyo rubber futures hit a two-week high on Thursday on expectations that main producer \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lift prices, but trading was slow ahead of a European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting on concerns a worsening economic outlook could curb demand.\par \par \uc2 FUNDAMENTALS\par \par \uc2 * The benchmark rubber contract on the Tokyo Commodity Exchange, June 2012, hit a high of 279.7 yen a kg, its strongest since Dec. 26, and was steady at 277 yen by 0101 GMT.\par \par \uc2 * Thailand could buy up to 200,000 tonnes of unsmoked rubber to push up prices to 120 baht ($3.79) per kg, from around 95 baht, after protests from farmers over low prices, government and farmers' officials said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 * Worries about the euro zone debt crisis mounted on Wednesday, after Fitch warned the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ramp up its debt purchases to avoid a "cataclysmic" collapse of the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , sinking the euro to its 16-month low against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 General Motors Co\uc2  could shift more vehicle production to its European factories in a cost-cutting deal with its German union that could avert a damaging standoff and keep Opel out of bankruptcy, people familiar with the discussions said.\par \par \uc2 * For a PDF of Reuters reports related to the producer meet, click: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/jus94s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/jus94s}}}\par \par \uc2 MARKET NEWS\par \par \uc2 * Japan's Nikkei average slipped in early trade on Thursday in a market that was nervous ahead of debt auctions this week in Spain and Italy after Fitch's warning of the collapse of the euro and renewed talk of a cut in France's triple-A ratings.\par \par \uc2 * U.S. gasoline futures briefly dipped below their 300-day moving average on Wednesday, dragged down by data showing a strong build in U.S. oil stocks and tepid demand.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (GMT) DATA/EVENTS  \tab \par  0130  China CPI yy                   Dec 2011    \par  \tab \par  0130  China PPI yy                   Dec 2011    \par  \tab \par  0530  India Industrial Output y/y    Nov 2011     \par  \tab \par  0900  Italy Industrial output yy WDA Nov 2011    \par  \tab \par  1000  EZ    Industrial production yy Nov 2011    \par  \tab \par  1200  Britain BOE Bank Rate          Jan 2012   \tab \par  1230  US     Retail sales             Dec 2011 \tab \par  1230  US     Jobless claims           Weekly   \tab \par  1245  EZ     ECB rate decision       Jan 2012   \par  \tab \par        Spain  Bond auction  \tab \par                     \tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Lewa Pardomuan; Editing by Sugita Katyal)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For morning and afternoon prices at Thailand's state-runcentral rubber market, click on <RUB-BKK3>.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For other physical rubber prices in Thailand, click on<RUB-BKK1> <RUB-BKK2>.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For more details on Indonesian and Malaysian prices click on and.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Reuters Terminal users can see cash and futures rubber pricesby double clicking on the codes in the brackets: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - Tokyo rubber futures -- <0#JRU:>\tab \par - Shanghai rubber futures      -- <0#SNR:>\tab \par - Singapore rubber futures     -- <0#SRS:><0#SRU:><0#STF:>\tab \par - Thai rubber futures          --  <0#ARU:><0#ASR20:>\tab \par - All rubber news             \tab \par - Tokyo rubber report         \tab \par - Shanghai rubber 