\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For September 26\b0\par\par\uc2 1,651 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 September 2011\par 09:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: PBOC GOV: CHINA WON'T CHANGE MONETARY, FISCAL POLICIES - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China doesn't expect to change its monetary or fiscal policies, but it must maintain flexibility in the event of a worsening of the global economy, China \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief was cited as saying. (published 0232 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: NEW ZEALAND AUGUST TRADE DEFICIT NZ$641 MILLION, WIDER THAN EXPECTED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand recorded a wider-than-expected August trade deficit as imports rose sharply, but economists expect the country to record an annual surplus through 2012. (published 0238 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: SINGAPORE AUGUST FACTORY OUTPUT RISES; \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MAY STILL EASE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's manufacturing output expanded for a third straight month in August due to a surge in the highly volatile pharmaceuticals sector, suggesting the economy may avert a recession despite heightened global uncertainties. (published 0646 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INTERVIEW: TAIWAN TO LOWER 2012 BORROWING ON HIGHER TAX REVENUE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's government plans to lower its borrowing by 30% next year due to an expected rise in tax revenues, a senior official from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said. (published 0414 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANK INDONESIA PLANS TO BUY IDR3 TLN GOVERNMENT BONDS TODAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia plans to buy IDR3 trillion worth of government bonds Monday to help support prices amid a heavy sell-off of emerging-market assets, an official at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said. (published 0624 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAI \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : READY TO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN CASE OF EXCESSIVE VOLATILITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stands ready to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market in case there is any excessive volatility in the movement of the baht, but so far the local unit has been moving in line with regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Deputy Governor Atchana Waiquamdee said Monday. (published 0603 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAI FINANCE MINISTRY: OCT-DEC GOVERNMENT BOND SUPPLY SET AT THB32B \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has set government bond supply for the first quarter of the next fiscal year, starting Oct. 1, at THB32 billion, much smaller than the THB125 billion scheduled for the current quarter, a senior ministry official said Monday. (published 0638 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  EXPECTS SEPTEMBER CPI RISE IN 3.8%-4.8% RANGE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Monday said it expects inflation, as measured by the consumer price index, to settle within the 3.8%-4.8% range in September. (published 0700 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par VIETNAM MINISTRY: 2011 TRADE DEFICIT WILL LIKELY NARROW TO $11 BILLION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam is likely to run a trade deficit of nearly $11 billion this year, narrower than last year's $12.4 billion deficit, the Ministry of Industry and Trade said Monday. (published 0409 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ASIA CEMENT TO SELL CNY586M 3-YEAR DIM SUM BONDS AT 2.95% INTEREST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asia Cement Holdings Corp. said Monday it has signed an agreement to sell CNY586 million of three-year yuan-denominated bonds in Hong Kong. (published 0045 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: BOJ TANKAN COULD SHOW REBOUND IN BUSINESS SENTIMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan's quarterly tankan survey due out next Monday will likely show a rebound in corporate sentiment, with the closely watched index for large manufacturers returning to positive territory from the previous quarter as production and exports have picked up. (published 0207 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par APPLE PUSHES FOR BAN OF SAMSUNG'S GALAXY 10.1 IN AUSTRALIA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An attorney representing \f28 \uc2 \f2 Apple Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . claimed in an Australian court Monday that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Samsung Electronics Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 's latest tablet computer infringes on patents relating to touch screen technology. (published 0501 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ALIBABA: TO SPIN OFF HICHINA GROUP LTD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese e-commerce portal \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alibaba.com Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday its non wholly-owned unit HiChina Group Ltd. is seeking a separate listing of its shares in the U.S. (published 0002 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ALIBABA'S HICHINA GROUP LIKELY VALUED AT AROUND US$500 MLN - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HiChina Group Ltd, a full-service Internet infrastructure service provider controlled by Chinese e-commerce portal \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alibaba.com Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . could be valued at around US$500 million, a source familiar with the situation said Monday, ahead of a separate listing in the U.S. (published 0245 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA YURUN PROFIT WARNING SENDS SHARES TO 33-MONTH LOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Yurun Food Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Monday issued a profit warning, saying its third-quarter net profit would decline as a result of higher raw material costs and media reports of contaminated pork. (published 0442 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PING AN: AWARE OF SHARE PRICE VOLATILITY; \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 OPERATIONS\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  NORMAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ping An Insurance Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . of China Ltd. said Monday it is aware of the volatility in the price of its Hong Kong-listed shares, and the company is operating normally. (published 0619 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HK GOVERNMENT INITIATES PROCEEDINGS AGAINST CHAODA MODERN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Hong Kong government has initiated proceedings against Chaoda Modern Agriculture Ltd., a government spokeswoman said Monday. (published 0704 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TCL MULTIMEDIA EXPECTS TO SWING TO THIRD-QUARTER NET PROFIT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese television maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 TCL Multimedia Technology Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday it expects to swing to a third-quarter and a January-September net profit from a year earlier. (published 0101 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GOVT-BACKED BODY: TEPCO TO FILE NEW COST-CUTTING PLAN BY END-OCT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A new government-backed body set up to help \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tokyo Electric Power Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . make compensation payments and resolve the crisis at the Fukushima Daiichi nuclear plant will file a new cost-cutting plan by the end of October, the body's head said Monday. (published 0507 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BOW ENERGY\f28 \uc2 \f2  RECOMMENDS SWEETENED A$534.6M SHELL, PETROCHINA OFFER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bow Energy Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . on Monday urged its shareholders to accept a sweetened A$534.6 million bid for the coal seam gas company by a joint venture between \f28 \uc2 \f2 Royal Dutch Shell PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and \f28 \uc2 \f2 PetroChina Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (published 2354 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ASTON RESOURCES MAIDEN FY NET PROFIT A$242.9 MILLION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Aston Resources Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Monday reported a maiden net profit for the year to June 30 of A$242.9 million, and said it expected to produce the first coal for sale from its Maules Creek deposit in the middle of 2013. (published 2238 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SAMSUNG ELECTRONICS\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO LAUNCH 2 GALAXY S SMARTPHONE MODELS WITH 4G NETWORK IN S KOREA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Samsung Electronics Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday it plans to launch in its home market two models of the second-generation version of its Galaxy S phone that will run on a faster network. (published 0150 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CBA CEO NORRIS SAYS NO NEED TO TAP MARKETS FOR FUNDING IN 2011 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Commonwealth Bank Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . outgoing chief executive Ralph Norris said Monday the bank doesn't need to raise funding during the remainder of the calendar year. (published 0301 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HALLENSTEIN GLASSON FY NET PROFIT NZ$18.3 MILLION, DOWN 6.6% VERSUS YEAR AGO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Clothes retailer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hallenstein Glasson Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Monday reported a lower fiscal-year net profit due to a warmer-than-expected winter and the impact of a series of earthquakes in New Zealand's second largest city of Christchurch. (published 2014 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RENEW WIND POWER GETS UP TO INR10 BLN FINANCING FROM GOLDMAN SACHS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indian renewable energy company ReNew Wind Power Pvt. Ltd. said Monday it has received up to INR10 billion in financing from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs Group Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (published 0656 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par LUPIN FINANCE CHIEF: MAY LEAVE REMAINING DOLLAR EXPOSURES OPEN IF RUPEE STAYS WEAK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Lupin Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . may go slow on hedging its dollar revenues as the rupee may not have bottomed out yet, a shift from its earlier view that the Indian unit was set to rise, a top executive said Monday. (published 0654 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES DROP AS EUROPE DEBT CONCERNS SHARPEN; EURO FALLS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets dropped in choppy trade Monday and the euro fell, as meetings by the world's finance ministers over the weekend did little to ease concerns over the European sovereign debt crisis. (published 0432 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OIL FUTURES: CRUDE FALLS TO SIX-WEEK LOW AMID BROAD SELLOFF \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude-oil futures fell to their lowest levels in six weeks amid a broader market selloff, as meetings among the world's finance ministers over the weekend did little to ease concerns over the European sovereign debt crisis. (published 0656 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 3RD UPDATE: CHEVRON, PARTNERS APPROVE US$29B WHEATSTONE LNG PROJECT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chevron Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and partners placed a US$29 billion bet on Asian demand for clean-burning fuels Monday by approving construction of the Wheatstone gas-export project in Australia, overlooking near-term worries about the global economy and competitive threats posed by new energy sources such as shale gas. (published 0644 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: SHANGHAI GOLD FUTURES FALL TO THEIR 5% LOWER LIMIT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Shanghai Futures Exchange gold futures fell to the 5% lower limi